1
00:00:26,044 --> 00:00:28,672
(METAL ELEVATOR DOOR CLOSING)

2
00:00:30,215 --> 00:00:33,885
(ELEVATOR ASCENDING)

3
00:00:44,563 --> 00:00:46,565
(ELEVATOR CREAKING)

4
00:00:46,773 --> 00:00:49,025
(GASPING)

5
00:00:49,109 --> 00:00:51,319
(COUGHING)

6
00:00:54,072 --> 00:00:55,991
(PANTING)

7
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:06,251
Hello?

8
00:01:06,543 --> 00:01:08,253
(COUGHING)

9
00:01:08,962 --> 00:01:10,297
Hello?
(SQUEALING)

10
00:01:14,509 --> 00:01:16,303
(LOW GROWLING)

11
00:01:19,598 --> 00:01:20,890
(SNARLS)

12
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:22,392
(GASPS)

13
00:01:25,979 --> 00:01:29,149
Hey! Hey! Help me!

14
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:31,693
(ELEVATOR ACCELERATING)

15
00:01:34,738 --> 00:01:36,156
(PANTING)

16
00:01:36,531 --> 00:01:37,824
(BUZZER SOUNDING)

17
00:01:38,783 --> 00:01:41,536
(PANTING CONTINUES)

18
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:59,804
(ALL LAUGHING)

19
00:02:05,143 --> 00:02:06,144
Go get him.

20
00:02:10,523 --> 00:02:11,691
Day one, Greenie.

21
00:02:11,858 --> 00:02:12,942
Rise and shine.

22
00:02:13,026 --> 00:02:14,361
(BOY LAUGHING)

23
00:02:14,444 --> 00:02:16,154
He looks like
a slopper to me.

24
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:17,989
(ALL CHATTERING)

25
00:02:18,073 --> 00:02:19,407
I could use some
help in the kitchen.

26
00:02:19,491 --> 00:02:22,118
(BOYS LAUGHING AND CHATTERING)

27
00:02:22,202 --> 00:02:24,412
(GRUNTING)
BOYS: (SHOUTING) Oh!

28
00:02:24,496 --> 00:02:26,081
Hey, we got a runner!

29
00:02:26,623 --> 00:02:28,333
(PANTING)

30
00:02:32,003 --> 00:02:33,129
(GROANS)

31
00:02:33,213 --> 00:02:34,589
BOYS: Oh!

32
00:02:34,673 --> 00:02:36,966
(ALL LAUGHING)

33
00:02:39,219 --> 00:02:40,595
(BOY WHOOPING)

34
00:02:42,389 --> 00:02:43,431
BOY 1: Take it all in.

35
00:02:45,183 --> 00:02:47,394
(BOYS CHEERING AND APPLAUDING)

36
00:02:48,937 --> 00:02:50,271
(GASPS)

37
00:03:12,919 --> 00:03:13,962
(GRUNTING)

38
00:03:16,089 --> 00:03:18,091
(LOCKS DOOR)

39
00:03:21,553 --> 00:03:22,887
BOY: He's all yours.

40
00:03:34,983 --> 00:03:36,067
Hey.

41
00:03:36,151 --> 00:03:37,277
(GASPS)

42
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:41,990
Hey there, Green Bean.

43
00:03:42,782 --> 00:03:44,784
You're not gonna
run again. Okay?

44
00:03:47,412 --> 00:03:48,413
Good.

45
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:50,290
(UNLOCKS DOOR)

46
00:03:53,668 --> 00:03:55,211
(CLEARS THROAT)

47
00:03:56,254 --> 00:03:57,589
My name is Alby.

48
00:03:59,257 --> 00:04:00,300
Can you tell me anything
about yourself?

49
00:04:00,383 --> 00:04:01,426
Who you are?

50
00:04:01,593 --> 00:04:04,596
Where you came from?
Anything at all.

51
00:04:09,642 --> 00:04:10,643
No.

52
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:12,479
Can you tell
me your name?

53
00:04:17,108 --> 00:04:19,068
I, uh, I can't
remember anything.

54
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:22,030
Why can't
I remember anything?

55
00:04:22,113 --> 00:04:23,072
It's okay.

56
00:04:23,156 --> 00:04:24,365
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

57
00:04:24,449 --> 00:04:25,742
Hey, relax.

58
00:04:26,075 --> 00:04:27,118
Relax.

59
00:04:28,119 --> 00:04:29,621
It's normal.

60
00:04:29,704 --> 00:04:30,705
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

61
00:04:30,789 --> 00:04:32,415
It happens to us all.

62
00:04:33,124 --> 00:04:35,126
You'll get your name
back in a day or two.

63
00:04:37,003 --> 00:04:39,130
It's the one thing
they let us keep.

64
00:04:42,926 --> 00:04:44,636
What is this place?

65
00:04:48,431 --> 00:04:49,432
Let me show you.

66
00:04:57,315 --> 00:04:59,067
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

67
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:00,860
ALBY: We eat here.

68
00:05:01,027 --> 00:05:02,362
We sleep here.

69
00:05:02,529 --> 00:05:03,905
We grow
our own food.

70
00:05:03,988 --> 00:05:05,490
We build
our own shelter.

71
00:05:06,491 --> 00:05:08,993
Whatever we need,
the Box provides.

72
00:05:09,077 --> 00:05:10,161
The rest
is up to us.

73
00:05:10,328 --> 00:05:11,496
The Box?

74
00:05:12,831 --> 00:05:14,791
Yeah. It's sent up
once a month

75
00:05:14,874 --> 00:05:17,210
with fresh supplies
and a new Greenie.

76
00:05:17,377 --> 00:05:18,837
This month
that's you.

77
00:05:19,045 --> 00:05:20,463
Congratulations.

78
00:05:22,549 --> 00:05:25,343
Sent up?
By who, though?
Who put us here?

79
00:05:26,302 --> 00:05:27,679
That, we don't know.

80
00:05:29,472 --> 00:05:31,182
Hey, are you
all right, Alby?
A-ha!

81
00:05:31,641 --> 00:05:33,184
Green Bean,
meet Newt.

82
00:05:33,351 --> 00:05:35,019
When I'm not around,
he's in charge.

83
00:05:35,186 --> 00:05:36,855
Well, it's a good thing
you're always around then.

84
00:05:37,021 --> 00:05:39,023
That was some dash
you made earlier.

85
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:42,068
For a second,
I thought you had the
chops to be a runner...

86
00:05:42,235 --> 00:05:44,028
...till you
face-planted.
(LAUGHS)

87
00:05:44,195 --> 00:05:45,363
That was great.

88
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:47,532
Wait, a "runner"?

89
00:05:47,699 --> 00:05:50,243
Newt, do me a favor.
Go find Chuck.

90
00:05:51,244 --> 00:05:52,704
All right.
Thanks.

91
00:05:54,873 --> 00:05:56,749
Look, I'm sorry
to rush this.

92
00:05:56,916 --> 00:06:00,044
You came up a little late,
and there's a lot to do.

93
00:06:00,211 --> 00:06:02,589
We got something special
planned tonight.

94
00:06:03,006 --> 00:06:05,008
Yeah. You'll see.

95
00:06:07,552 --> 00:06:09,721
I hope you're not
afraid of heights.

96
00:06:09,888 --> 00:06:11,890
Let's go. Come on.

97
00:06:17,562 --> 00:06:19,272
This is
all we got.

98
00:06:21,566 --> 00:06:23,276
We've worked
hard for it.

99
00:06:24,402 --> 00:06:25,695
If you respect
this place...

100
00:06:26,779 --> 00:06:28,740
you and I will
get along just fine.

101
00:06:29,073 --> 00:06:30,617
What's out there?

102
00:06:41,085 --> 00:06:42,754
We only have
three rules.

103
00:06:43,922 --> 00:06:46,424
First, do your part.

104
00:06:47,258 --> 00:06:49,093
No time for
any freeloaders.

105
00:06:50,178 --> 00:06:52,931
Second, never
harm another Glader.

106
00:06:53,097 --> 00:06:55,183
None of this works
unless we have trust.

107
00:06:56,935 --> 00:06:58,603
Most importantly...

108
00:06:59,729 --> 00:07:02,023
never go beyond
those walls.

109
00:07:03,733 --> 00:07:05,777
Do you understand
me, Greenie?

110
00:07:07,278 --> 00:07:08,529
CHUCK: Hey, Alby!

111
00:07:13,284 --> 00:07:15,912
Hey, Chuck.
Where you been, man?

112
00:07:17,622 --> 00:07:20,375
It's basically the same
story for all of us.

113
00:07:21,292 --> 00:07:24,629
We wake up in the Box,
Alby gives us the tour...

114
00:07:25,546 --> 00:07:27,131
then here we are.

115
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:30,969
Don't worry.

116
00:07:31,135 --> 00:07:33,096
You're already
doing better than I did.

117
00:07:33,888 --> 00:07:35,348
I clunked
my pants three times

118
00:07:35,431 --> 00:07:37,392
before they got
me out of the pit.

119
00:07:40,895 --> 00:07:42,605
No, come on.

120
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:51,155
Dude, where
are you going?

121
00:07:51,322 --> 00:07:52,490
I just wanna see.

122
00:07:52,991 --> 00:07:54,158
You can look
around all you want

123
00:07:54,242 --> 00:07:55,827
but you better
not go out there.

124
00:07:55,994 --> 00:07:57,453
Why not?
What's through there?

125
00:07:57,620 --> 00:08:00,331
I don't know.
I just know
what I'm told.

126
00:08:00,498 --> 00:08:01,833
And we're not
supposed to leave.

127
00:08:03,042 --> 00:08:04,502
(SIGHS)

128
00:08:11,801 --> 00:08:14,178
BEN: Hey, Chuck.
New Greenie, huh?

129
00:08:14,762 --> 00:08:16,180
How does it feel
to be promoted?

130
00:08:16,514 --> 00:08:17,807
Feels great, Ben.

131
00:08:19,308 --> 00:08:21,352
I thought no one
was allowed to leave.

132
00:08:21,519 --> 00:08:23,312
I said we're not
allowed to leave.

133
00:08:23,479 --> 00:08:24,939
They're different,
they're runners.

134
00:08:25,023 --> 00:08:26,816
They know more about
the maze than anyone.

135
00:08:26,983 --> 00:08:28,276
Wait, what?

136
00:08:28,443 --> 00:08:29,694
What?

137
00:08:29,861 --> 00:08:31,696
What? You just
said "maze."

138
00:08:32,363 --> 00:08:33,698
I did?

139
00:08:33,865 --> 00:08:34,866
Yeah.

140
00:08:37,869 --> 00:08:40,204
Where are you going?
What are you doing?

141
00:08:40,371 --> 00:08:41,539
I'm just gonna
take a look.

142
00:08:41,706 --> 00:08:43,166
I told you,
you can't.

143
00:08:43,249 --> 00:08:45,877
No one leaves,
especially not now.

144
00:08:47,045 --> 00:08:48,171
It's not safe.

145
00:08:48,713 --> 00:08:50,548
Okay, all right,
I'm not gonna go.

146
00:08:59,182 --> 00:09:00,141
Hey!

147
00:09:00,224 --> 00:09:02,185
(GRUNTS)
(WHIMPERS)

148
00:09:03,895 --> 00:09:05,229
We gotta
stop meeting
like this, Greenie.

149
00:09:05,396 --> 00:09:06,606
Get off me!

150
00:09:06,689 --> 00:09:07,815
All right!
Calm, calm, calm.

151
00:09:07,982 --> 00:09:08,983
BOY: Don't touch me!

152
00:09:09,067 --> 00:09:10,735
GALLY: Whoa! Take it easy!

153
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:11,861
Just relax.

154
00:09:12,028 --> 00:09:13,654
What the hell is
wrong with you guys?

155
00:09:13,821 --> 00:09:14,864
Just calm down,
all right?

156
00:09:15,031 --> 00:09:16,991
No, okay?
Why won't you tell
me what's out there?

157
00:09:17,075 --> 00:09:18,576
We're just
trying to protect you.
It's for your own good.

158
00:09:18,743 --> 00:09:19,744
You guys can't
just keep me here.

159
00:09:19,911 --> 00:09:21,829
I can't let you leave.
Why not?

160
00:09:22,288 --> 00:09:24,540
(FAINT CLICK)

161
00:09:26,751 --> 00:09:28,669
(HEAVY THUD)

162
00:09:30,755 --> 00:09:33,007
(WIND WHOOSHING)

163
00:09:39,472 --> 00:09:40,515
(PANTING)

164
00:09:40,598 --> 00:09:41,891
What the hell?

165
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:45,603
(GEARS TURNING)

166
00:10:07,458 --> 00:10:10,503
Next time,
I'm gonna
let you leave.

167
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,802
Welcome to the Glade.

168
00:10:25,518 --> 00:10:27,353
(DRUMS PLAYING)

169
00:10:28,354 --> 00:10:29,355
Light him up!

170
00:10:30,815 --> 00:10:32,316
(ALL CHEERING)

171
00:10:44,871 --> 00:10:46,414
(WHOOPING)

172
00:10:47,373 --> 00:10:48,374
(LAUGHS)

173
00:10:59,844 --> 00:11:00,887
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

174
00:11:00,970 --> 00:11:02,972
Hell of a
first day, Greenie.

175
00:11:05,683 --> 00:11:06,684
Here.

176
00:11:07,685 --> 00:11:08,936
Put some hair
on your chest.

177
00:11:15,526 --> 00:11:16,777
(SPITS) Oh!

178
00:11:16,861 --> 00:11:18,613
(LAUGHS)
(COUGHING)

179
00:11:18,696 --> 00:11:20,948
Oh, my God!
What is that?

180
00:11:21,616 --> 00:11:24,118
(CONTINUES COUGHING)

181
00:11:24,410 --> 00:11:25,578
I don't
even know.

182
00:11:27,038 --> 00:11:28,581
It's Gally's recipe.

183
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:30,791
It's a trade secret.

184
00:11:30,875 --> 00:11:32,835
(BOYS SHOUTING)

185
00:11:32,919 --> 00:11:34,795
Yeah, well,
he's still an asshole.

186
00:11:35,713 --> 00:11:37,423
He saved
your life today.

187
00:11:40,051 --> 00:11:42,970
Trust me. The maze
is a dangerous place.

188
00:11:49,435 --> 00:11:51,896
We're trapped here,
aren't we?

189
00:11:53,481 --> 00:11:54,774
For the moment.

190
00:11:57,652 --> 00:11:58,736
But...

191
00:11:59,737 --> 00:12:00,780
you see those guys?

192
00:12:01,572 --> 00:12:03,115
There, by the fire?

193
00:12:04,075 --> 00:12:05,618
Those are the runners.

194
00:12:05,993 --> 00:12:08,829
That guy in the middle
there, that's Minho.

195
00:12:09,789 --> 00:12:11,332
He's the Keeper
of the Runners.

196
00:12:11,499 --> 00:12:15,253
Every morning,
when those doors open,
they run the maze...

197
00:12:15,419 --> 00:12:17,380
mapping it,
memorizing it,

198
00:12:17,463 --> 00:12:18,756
trying to
find a way out.

199
00:12:20,091 --> 00:12:21,759
How long have
they been looking?

200
00:12:23,094 --> 00:12:24,345
Three years.

201
00:12:27,265 --> 00:12:28,766
And they haven't
found anything?

202
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:31,352
It's a lot
easier said than done.

203
00:12:33,104 --> 00:12:34,272
Listen.

204
00:12:35,773 --> 00:12:38,401
(DISTANT CREAKING)

205
00:12:38,484 --> 00:12:39,568
Hear that?

206
00:12:40,278 --> 00:12:42,863
It's the maze,
changing.

207
00:12:44,407 --> 00:12:45,825
It changes
every night.

208
00:12:46,993 --> 00:12:48,953
How is that
even possible?

209
00:12:50,162 --> 00:12:51,580
You can ask the people
who put us in here,

210
00:12:51,664 --> 00:12:53,791
if you ever
meet the bastards.

211
00:12:56,752 --> 00:12:58,963
Listen,
the truth is...

212
00:12:59,130 --> 00:13:00,589
the runners
are the only ones

213
00:13:00,673 --> 00:13:02,133
who really know
what's out there.

214
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,468
They are the
strongest and the
fastest of us all.

215
00:13:04,552 --> 00:13:05,553
And it's a good
thing, too...

216
00:13:05,636 --> 00:13:07,722
because if they
don't make it back before
those doors close...

217
00:13:07,888 --> 00:13:09,807
then they are
stuck out there
for the night.

218
00:13:11,767 --> 00:13:14,353
And no one
has ever survived
a night in the maze.

219
00:13:19,984 --> 00:13:21,610
What happens
to them?

220
00:13:25,573 --> 00:13:27,533
Well, we call
them Grievers.

221
00:13:29,201 --> 00:13:31,912
Of course, no one's
ever seen one

222
00:13:31,996 --> 00:13:33,456
and lived to
tell about it.

223
00:13:35,374 --> 00:13:37,001
But they're out there.

224
00:13:42,631 --> 00:13:44,884
Right, that's enough
questions for one night.

225
00:13:44,967 --> 00:13:45,968
Come on.

226
00:13:46,135 --> 00:13:48,679
You're supposed to
be the guest of honor.

227
00:13:48,763 --> 00:13:50,514
Oh, no...
No! No, come on.

228
00:13:50,598 --> 00:13:52,016
Let me show you around.

229
00:13:52,892 --> 00:13:53,934
Come on.

230
00:13:54,352 --> 00:13:55,978
(GRUNTING)

231
00:13:56,062 --> 00:13:58,147
ALL: (CHEERING)
Whoa!

232
00:13:58,230 --> 00:13:59,774
And there
we got the builders.

233
00:14:00,232 --> 00:14:01,567
They're very good
with their hands...

234
00:14:01,734 --> 00:14:03,652
but not a lot
going on upstairs.

235
00:14:04,195 --> 00:14:05,738
And then
we got Winston...

236
00:14:06,155 --> 00:14:08,115
he's the Keeper
of the Slicers.

237
00:14:08,824 --> 00:14:10,618
And we got
two med-jacks,
Clint and Jeff.

238
00:14:10,785 --> 00:14:12,328
Hey, what's up?
Yo, Newt.

239
00:14:12,870 --> 00:14:15,498
They spend most
of their time bandaging
up the slicers.

240
00:14:15,831 --> 00:14:17,583
What if I want
to be a runner?

241
00:14:17,666 --> 00:14:18,667
(CHUCKLES)

242
00:14:18,751 --> 00:14:19,960
Have you listened to
a word I've just said?

243
00:14:20,044 --> 00:14:21,670
No one wants
to be a runner.

244
00:14:21,962 --> 00:14:23,923
And, besides,
you gotta get chosen.

245
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:25,132
Chosen by who?

246
00:14:25,216 --> 00:14:26,634
(GROANS)
BOYS: Whoa!

247
00:14:31,639 --> 00:14:32,765
What do you
say, Greenie?

248
00:14:32,932 --> 00:14:34,600
Wanna see what
you're made of?

249
00:14:34,767 --> 00:14:37,645
(ALL CHANTING)
Greenie! Greenie! Greenie!

250
00:14:41,065 --> 00:14:43,192
(CHANTING CONTINUES)

251
00:14:48,906 --> 00:14:50,950
(ALL CHEERING)

252
00:14:55,746 --> 00:14:57,373
Okay. All right.

253
00:14:58,290 --> 00:15:00,126
The rules are
simple, Greenie.

254
00:15:00,292 --> 00:15:01,836
I try to push you
out of the circle...

255
00:15:02,711 --> 00:15:04,839
you try to last more
than five seconds.
(ALL LAUGHING)

256
00:15:04,964 --> 00:15:06,799
BOY 1: Take it
easy on the Greenie.
GALLY: Ready?

257
00:15:07,925 --> 00:15:09,802
(GRUNTING)
(BOYS SHOUTING)

258
00:15:11,929 --> 00:15:13,222
(COUGHS)

259
00:15:13,514 --> 00:15:14,682
BOY 2: Get up, boy.

260
00:15:14,849 --> 00:15:17,059
Come on, Greenie.
We're not done yet.

261
00:15:19,687 --> 00:15:20,813
Stop calling me Greenie.

262
00:15:21,355 --> 00:15:22,356
GALLY:
Stop calling you that?

263
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:25,025
What do you wanna
be called? Shank?

264
00:15:25,109 --> 00:15:27,820
(BOYS LAUGHING AND CHEERING)

265
00:15:27,903 --> 00:15:29,029
What do you
think, boys?

266
00:15:29,113 --> 00:15:30,573
Does he look
like a Shank?

267
00:15:35,494 --> 00:15:36,662
(BOTH GRUNTING)

268
00:15:36,745 --> 00:15:37,997
BOYS: Whoa!

269
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,081
BOY 3: Come on!

270
00:15:39,874 --> 00:15:41,959
You know what?
I think I've settled
on Shank.

271
00:15:42,042 --> 00:15:44,211
(BOYS LAUGHING)

272
00:15:51,969 --> 00:15:52,970
BOYS: Oh!

273
00:15:53,053 --> 00:15:54,472
There you go,
Greenie!

274
00:15:57,683 --> 00:15:58,893
Not bad for
a Greenie, huh?

275
00:16:00,394 --> 00:16:01,479
Oh! (COUGHS)

276
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:04,356
(BOYS CHATTERING)

277
00:16:08,235 --> 00:16:09,236
Thomas.

278
00:16:10,738 --> 00:16:12,281
Thomas. Hey!

279
00:16:13,157 --> 00:16:14,158
Thomas!

280
00:16:15,493 --> 00:16:16,494
(THOMAS LAUGHS)

281
00:16:17,077 --> 00:16:19,538
I remember my name.
I'm Thomas!

282
00:16:21,582 --> 00:16:22,583
ALL: Thomas!

283
00:16:25,044 --> 00:16:26,879
(ALL CHEERING)

284
00:16:27,296 --> 00:16:28,756
Welcome home, Thomas.

285
00:16:31,342 --> 00:16:33,469
(INAUDIBLE)

286
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:42,144
Good job... Thomas.

287
00:16:43,312 --> 00:16:45,606
(DISTANT ROARING)

288
00:16:50,861 --> 00:16:52,154
What the hell
was that?

289
00:16:54,156 --> 00:16:56,992
That, my friend,
was a Griever.

290
00:16:58,661 --> 00:17:01,288
Don't worry,
you're safe
here with us.

291
00:17:02,331 --> 00:17:04,124
Nothing gets
through those walls.

292
00:17:05,084 --> 00:17:06,085
All right, guys.

293
00:17:06,210 --> 00:17:08,254
Let's tuck it in for
the night. Come on.

294
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:09,755
It was a good night.

295
00:17:11,131 --> 00:17:12,341
Good job, man.

296
00:17:42,955 --> 00:17:43,956
GALLY:
<i>You're safe here with us.</i>

297
00:17:44,081 --> 00:17:45,332
WOMAN: <i>Wicked is good.</i>

298
00:17:45,416 --> 00:17:46,458
THOMAS: <i>What's out there?</i>

299
00:17:46,542 --> 00:17:48,210
GIRL: <i>Thomas, Thomas.</i>

300
00:17:51,463 --> 00:17:52,673
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

301
00:17:53,799 --> 00:17:55,301
<i>Everything is going to change.</i>

302
00:17:57,928 --> 00:17:58,929
ALBY: Thomas.

303
00:17:59,722 --> 00:18:00,764
Shh.

304
00:18:04,852 --> 00:18:06,103
Follow me.

305
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:14,695
ALBY: It's peaceful, isn't it?

306
00:18:16,155 --> 00:18:18,907
I know it's hard to believe,
but it wasn't always this way.

307
00:18:20,326 --> 00:18:22,036
We had dark days.

308
00:18:23,579 --> 00:18:25,873
We lost a lot of boys to fear.

309
00:18:26,332 --> 00:18:27,666
To panic.

310
00:18:29,168 --> 00:18:31,003
We've come
far since then.

311
00:18:32,588 --> 00:18:34,089
Established
order...

312
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:36,383
made peace.

313
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,596
Yeah. Why are
you telling me this?

314
00:18:41,013 --> 00:18:42,848
Because you're not
like the others.

315
00:18:44,767 --> 00:18:46,310
You're curious.

316
00:18:46,977 --> 00:18:48,771
But you're
one of us now.

317
00:18:49,938 --> 00:18:51,899
You need to know
what that means.

318
00:19:14,463 --> 00:19:16,131
What happened
to them?

319
00:19:17,049 --> 00:19:18,425
Like I said...

320
00:19:20,094 --> 00:19:21,679
dark days,
Thomas.

321
00:19:35,859 --> 00:19:37,861
Has anyone tried
climbing to the top?

322
00:19:39,113 --> 00:19:42,282
Tried it. The ivy
doesn't go all
the way to the top.

323
00:19:42,658 --> 00:19:44,660
And besides,
where are you gonna
go from there?

324
00:19:45,786 --> 00:19:46,829
And what
about the Box?

325
00:19:46,912 --> 00:19:48,122
You know, next
time it comes up...

326
00:19:48,288 --> 00:19:49,832
No, we tried that.

327
00:19:49,998 --> 00:19:51,792
The Box won't
go back down with
someone in it.

328
00:19:52,126 --> 00:19:53,210
Okay, what if we...

329
00:19:53,293 --> 00:19:54,503
No, we tried it,
all right?

330
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:55,879
Twice.

331
00:19:56,880 --> 00:20:00,801
All right? Trust me.
Anything you think of,
we've already tried.

332
00:20:02,261 --> 00:20:04,471
The only way
out of here is
through the maze.

333
00:20:05,639 --> 00:20:07,474
Now, look,
you wanna be helpful?

334
00:20:09,017 --> 00:20:10,018
Here.

335
00:20:10,102 --> 00:20:12,020
Go dig us up
some more fertilizer.

336
00:20:20,696 --> 00:20:23,198
"Just get the fertilizer,
Thomas."

337
00:20:23,365 --> 00:20:26,326
"Are you sure, guys?
I can't help in
any other way?"

338
00:20:26,493 --> 00:20:28,620
"No, just get
the fertilizer.

339
00:20:29,913 --> 00:20:32,458
"You know where it is.
It's just out in the
middle of the woods."

340
00:21:07,284 --> 00:21:09,369
(FLIES BUZZING)

341
00:21:09,578 --> 00:21:11,038
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

342
00:21:12,289 --> 00:21:13,290
Oh!

343
00:21:14,583 --> 00:21:16,251
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

344
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:17,461
Uh...

345
00:21:18,545 --> 00:21:19,546
You're Ben, right?

346
00:21:19,713 --> 00:21:21,465
I don't know
if we ever...
(GRUNTING)

347
00:21:23,467 --> 00:21:24,468
Are you okay?

348
00:21:26,136 --> 00:21:28,055
(SHOUTS)
(GROANS)

349
00:21:28,138 --> 00:21:29,556
Get the hell off me!

350
00:21:30,057 --> 00:21:31,600
It's your fault.

351
00:21:31,767 --> 00:21:33,143
I saw you.

352
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:34,645
You did this.

353
00:21:34,812 --> 00:21:36,188
I saw you!

354
00:21:36,271 --> 00:21:37,397
(BOTH GRUNTING)

355
00:21:37,481 --> 00:21:38,482
(SCREAMS)

356
00:21:38,816 --> 00:21:40,317
(CHOKING)

357
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:43,195
(GASPING)

358
00:21:59,461 --> 00:22:02,089
Hey! Hey!

359
00:22:06,885 --> 00:22:08,428
THOMAS: Hey!

360
00:22:09,388 --> 00:22:11,056
Help!

361
00:22:11,557 --> 00:22:13,642
Help! Help!

362
00:22:15,185 --> 00:22:16,186
Help!

363
00:22:22,192 --> 00:22:23,193
I'll kill you!

364
00:22:23,277 --> 00:22:24,278
(BOYS SHOUTING)

365
00:22:24,361 --> 00:22:25,696
(SCREAMS)
NEWT: Hey!

366
00:22:28,031 --> 00:22:29,408
Hold him down.

367
00:22:29,575 --> 00:22:31,326
What are you doing?
(GRUNTING)

368
00:22:31,410 --> 00:22:32,494
Calm down, Ben.

369
00:22:32,703 --> 00:22:33,871
What the hell happened?

370
00:22:34,037 --> 00:22:35,038
He just attacked me!

371
00:22:35,122 --> 00:22:36,123
Are you okay?

372
00:22:36,206 --> 00:22:37,207
(MOANING)

373
00:22:37,291 --> 00:22:38,292
GALLY: Calm down, Ben.

374
00:22:41,753 --> 00:22:43,338
No. No.

375
00:22:44,089 --> 00:22:45,632
All right,
lift his shirt.

376
00:22:45,799 --> 00:22:47,759
Lift his shirt.
(GROANING) No! No!

377
00:22:47,926 --> 00:22:50,095
No! No!
Please. Please.

378
00:22:50,178 --> 00:22:51,179
(BEN PANTING)

379
00:22:53,181 --> 00:22:54,600
He's been stung.

380
00:22:55,726 --> 00:22:56,935
In the middle
of the day?

381
00:22:58,770 --> 00:23:00,105
Help me, please.

382
00:23:00,272 --> 00:23:01,481
(CRYING) Please.

383
00:23:01,565 --> 00:23:03,066
Please, just help.

384
00:23:03,567 --> 00:23:04,568
(SIGHS)

385
00:23:04,651 --> 00:23:05,652
Put him in the pit.

386
00:23:05,819 --> 00:23:07,237
GALLY: Everybody, help.
Take him to the pit.

387
00:23:07,404 --> 00:23:08,989
No!
Med-jack!

388
00:23:09,072 --> 00:23:10,449
Please don't do it!

389
00:23:11,241 --> 00:23:12,284
Calm down, Ben.

390
00:23:12,451 --> 00:23:13,619
Back down, Ben.

391
00:23:13,994 --> 00:23:15,871
Listen to me! Please!

392
00:23:17,122 --> 00:23:19,082
(BEN SCREAMING)

393
00:23:19,166 --> 00:23:20,959
Please, stop, please!

394
00:23:21,293 --> 00:23:22,669
He did this!

395
00:23:22,836 --> 00:23:25,589
Please stop! No!
No, please! Help me!

396
00:23:25,756 --> 00:23:27,257
THOMAS:
<i>So what happened to him?</i>

397
00:23:30,886 --> 00:23:33,013
It's called
"The Changing."

398
00:23:34,222 --> 00:23:37,142
It's what happens
when someone gets stung.

399
00:23:39,019 --> 00:23:40,103
Listen.

400
00:23:45,859 --> 00:23:47,319
We haven't been able
to get a clear word

401
00:23:47,402 --> 00:23:49,237
out of Ben
since it happened.

402
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:52,240
He's not making
any sense.

403
00:23:52,991 --> 00:23:55,494
And it's only
gonna get worse.

404
00:23:55,661 --> 00:23:57,746
The infection
is spreading.

405
00:23:57,829 --> 00:23:59,623
He's dangerous.

406
00:24:02,167 --> 00:24:04,211
What did
he say to you?

407
00:24:10,467 --> 00:24:13,345
He said he saw me...

408
00:24:13,512 --> 00:24:15,597
and that this
was all my fault.

409
00:24:17,975 --> 00:24:20,143
How could this
be my fault?

410
00:24:26,441 --> 00:24:27,859
Get some rest.

411
00:24:29,277 --> 00:24:30,737
Alby?
Yeah.

412
00:24:32,155 --> 00:24:33,657
What's gonna
happen to him?

413
00:24:48,839 --> 00:24:52,175
(BREATHING HEAVILY)
Just listen to me.
Just, please, listen to me!

414
00:24:52,342 --> 00:24:53,844
Please, Minho!

415
00:24:54,136 --> 00:24:55,345
(GROWLING)

416
00:24:56,054 --> 00:24:57,055
Alby!

417
00:25:02,936 --> 00:25:05,230
(BEN CONTINUES GROWLING)

418
00:25:08,608 --> 00:25:11,028
(WHEEZING)

419
00:25:12,904 --> 00:25:15,449
(SOBBING)

420
00:25:16,450 --> 00:25:18,702
(COUGHING)

421
00:25:22,873 --> 00:25:26,209
No, please.
Please, don't.

422
00:25:26,376 --> 00:25:27,586
Please, don't do it.

423
00:25:31,131 --> 00:25:32,883
(BEN SOBBING)

424
00:25:33,759 --> 00:25:36,094
(GEARS TURNING)

425
00:25:39,598 --> 00:25:41,224
(WIND WHOOSHING)

426
00:25:41,308 --> 00:25:42,642
(WHIMPERING)

427
00:25:43,435 --> 00:25:44,478
Poles!

428
00:25:50,901 --> 00:25:52,319
(GROWLING)

429
00:25:54,780 --> 00:25:56,073
Move in!

430
00:25:57,074 --> 00:25:59,117
No, no, no! Please!

431
00:25:59,993 --> 00:26:02,746
No, please!
Please, don't!

432
00:26:02,913 --> 00:26:05,791
I can get better!
Please, just listen to me!

433
00:26:06,249 --> 00:26:07,751
Please, stop, please!

434
00:26:09,503 --> 00:26:11,004
ALBY: Push him in!
Stop!

435
00:26:11,088 --> 00:26:12,506
(BEN CRYING)

436
00:26:12,589 --> 00:26:14,007
I'll get better!

437
00:26:15,467 --> 00:26:17,511
(BOYS GRUNTING)
(WHIMPERING)

438
00:26:17,594 --> 00:26:19,012
(SOBBING)

439
00:26:21,223 --> 00:26:22,766
(PLEADING)

440
00:26:24,726 --> 00:26:26,394
(SCREAMING)

441
00:26:49,709 --> 00:26:51,545
He belongs
to the maze now.

442
00:27:30,333 --> 00:27:32,169
THOMAS:
Do you think he might make it?

443
00:27:34,671 --> 00:27:36,131
Ben?

444
00:27:38,008 --> 00:27:39,467
No.

445
00:27:40,844 --> 00:27:43,513
No one survives
a night in the maze.

446
00:27:47,350 --> 00:27:49,561
We just gotta
forget about him.

447
00:28:19,382 --> 00:28:20,842
GIRL: <i>Thomas.</i>

448
00:28:21,843 --> 00:28:23,887
WOMAN: <i>Wicked is good.</i>

449
00:28:24,387 --> 00:28:25,847
<i>Don't make it easy on them.</i>

450
00:28:26,681 --> 00:28:29,059
GIRL: <i>Thomas.</i>

451
00:28:29,226 --> 00:28:31,895
<i>Everything is going to change.</i>

452
00:28:33,605 --> 00:28:35,273
THOMAS: <i>Wicked is good.</i>

453
00:28:38,068 --> 00:28:39,736
MALE SCIENTIST:
<i>This is gonna hurt a little.</i>

454
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:43,114
WOMAN: <i>Wicked is good.</i>

455
00:28:43,281 --> 00:28:45,951
<i>Thomas, you have to choose.</i>

456
00:28:48,078 --> 00:28:50,413
(GEARS TURNING)

457
00:29:14,271 --> 00:29:16,481
THOMAS:
But why would Alby
go into the maze?

458
00:29:16,815 --> 00:29:18,984
I mean,
he's not a runner.

459
00:29:19,150 --> 00:29:20,610
NEWT: Things
are different now.

460
00:29:20,819 --> 00:29:23,113
Alby went to
retrace Ben's footsteps
before sundown.

461
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:24,281
Are you gonna help?

462
00:29:24,447 --> 00:29:26,408
So he's gonna
go back to where
Ben was just stung...

463
00:29:26,574 --> 00:29:27,784
Alby knows
what he's doing...

464
00:29:28,118 --> 00:29:29,286
all right?

465
00:29:29,452 --> 00:29:30,954
He knows better
than any of us.

466
00:29:32,789 --> 00:29:34,457
What does
that mean?

467
00:29:38,211 --> 00:29:40,422
Well, it's like
you have heard, yeah?

468
00:29:40,588 --> 00:29:43,550
Every month,
the Box sends
up a new arrival.

469
00:29:43,717 --> 00:29:45,302
But someone had
to be first, right?

470
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:50,557
Someone had to have
spent a whole month
in the Glade, alone.

471
00:29:52,142 --> 00:29:54,060
That was Alby.

472
00:29:55,645 --> 00:29:57,731
I mean,
it can't have been easy.

473
00:29:57,897 --> 00:29:59,065
But when those
other boys started

474
00:29:59,149 --> 00:30:00,734
coming up,
one after the other...

475
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:02,902
he saw the truth.

476
00:30:03,069 --> 00:30:05,280
And he learned
that the most
important thing...

477
00:30:05,447 --> 00:30:07,282
is that we all
have each other.

478
00:30:09,284 --> 00:30:11,411
Because we're all
in this together.

479
00:30:29,971 --> 00:30:31,014
Yeah.

480
00:30:32,098 --> 00:30:33,767
There you go,
Greenie.

481
00:30:39,439 --> 00:30:41,775
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

482
00:30:57,665 --> 00:30:59,793
THOMAS:
They should be back by now.

483
00:31:00,502 --> 00:31:02,379
What happens if
they don't make it?

484
00:31:03,046 --> 00:31:04,714
They're gonna
make it.

485
00:31:07,175 --> 00:31:08,843
What happens
if they don't?

486
00:31:09,886 --> 00:31:11,554
They're gonna
make it.

487
00:31:44,879 --> 00:31:46,673
Come on, guys,
can't we send
someone after them?

488
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:48,216
GALLY:
That's against the rules.

489
00:31:48,925 --> 00:31:51,261
Either they make it
back or they don't.

490
00:31:51,886 --> 00:31:54,264
We can't risk
losing anyone else.

491
00:31:57,976 --> 00:31:59,936
(WIND WHOOSHING)

492
00:32:05,191 --> 00:32:06,609
Oh, no.

493
00:32:06,985 --> 00:32:08,653
(BOYS MURMURING)

494
00:32:09,779 --> 00:32:10,780
There!

495
00:32:10,864 --> 00:32:12,407
(MINHO GRUNTING LOUDLY)

496
00:32:13,950 --> 00:32:15,118
Wait,
something's wrong.

497
00:32:16,119 --> 00:32:17,120
(GRUNTING)

498
00:32:17,454 --> 00:32:19,122
Come on, Minho,
you can do it!

499
00:32:19,289 --> 00:32:21,374
ALL: Come on! Go!

500
00:32:23,626 --> 00:32:25,295
CHUCK: Come on,
you can make it!

501
00:32:25,462 --> 00:32:26,963
Minho, you gotta
leave him!

502
00:32:27,130 --> 00:32:28,715
They're not
gonna make it.

503
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:30,925
(BOYS SHOUTING)
You gotta
leave him!

504
00:32:32,177 --> 00:32:33,261
(YELLING)

505
00:32:34,804 --> 00:32:37,849
(INAUDIBLE)

506
00:32:49,110 --> 00:32:50,320
CHUCK: Thomas, no!

507
00:32:51,488 --> 00:32:53,698
(THOMAS GRUNTING)

508
00:32:53,781 --> 00:32:55,200
(BOYS SHOUTING)

509
00:32:56,868 --> 00:32:58,161
(PANTING)

510
00:33:05,502 --> 00:33:06,628
Good job.

511
00:33:08,296 --> 00:33:10,298
You just
killed yourself.

512
00:33:12,133 --> 00:33:13,259
What?

513
00:33:18,598 --> 00:33:20,683
(PANTING)

514
00:33:26,689 --> 00:33:28,358
What happened
to him?

515
00:33:28,942 --> 00:33:30,193
What does it
look like?

516
00:33:31,319 --> 00:33:33,029
He got stung.

517
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:36,032
What happened
to his head?

518
00:33:37,492 --> 00:33:39,702
I did what
I had to do.

519
00:33:44,624 --> 00:33:47,293
(DISTANT ROARING)

520
00:33:48,461 --> 00:33:50,505
(GRUNTING)

521
00:33:52,048 --> 00:33:54,801
Okay. Okay,
help me get him up.

522
00:33:54,968 --> 00:33:57,220
We gotta go.
The maze is
already changing.

523
00:33:57,387 --> 00:33:58,846
Hey, Minho!

524
00:34:01,724 --> 00:34:03,851
We can't just
leave him here.

525
00:34:16,197 --> 00:34:18,074
THOMAS: We gotta get him up.

526
00:34:18,241 --> 00:34:19,951
(BOTH GRUNTING)

527
00:34:25,081 --> 00:34:26,541
Come on.

528
00:34:37,093 --> 00:34:39,262
Just sit him down.
Sit him down.

529
00:34:47,270 --> 00:34:49,272
(DISTANT ROARING)

530
00:34:52,275 --> 00:34:54,652
This isn't going to work.
We gotta go.

531
00:34:54,819 --> 00:34:55,862
We gotta go!

532
00:34:56,029 --> 00:34:58,323
Wait,
what are you talking about?
We gotta hide him.

533
00:34:58,489 --> 00:34:59,616
Where?
I don't know.

534
00:34:59,782 --> 00:35:02,452
Are you telling me
there's not a single place
we could take him?

535
00:35:02,535 --> 00:35:03,536
(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)

536
00:35:05,079 --> 00:35:06,789
Listen to me,
shuck-face, all right.

537
00:35:06,956 --> 00:35:10,418
Take a look around.
There's nowhere to go!

538
00:35:10,501 --> 00:35:12,128
(BOTH PANTING)

539
00:35:15,882 --> 00:35:17,383
You don't get it.

540
00:35:18,259 --> 00:35:19,552
We're already dead.

541
00:35:37,654 --> 00:35:39,364
(GRUNTING)

542
00:35:41,157 --> 00:35:42,784
Two, three...

543
00:35:42,867 --> 00:35:44,911
(BOTH GRUNTING)

544
00:35:47,997 --> 00:35:49,499
Two, three...

545
00:35:53,378 --> 00:35:54,504
Okay.

546
00:35:54,587 --> 00:35:56,798
(MAZE WALLS SHIFTING)

547
00:35:56,881 --> 00:35:58,424
What are you doing?
What are you doing?

548
00:36:01,344 --> 00:36:02,512
What are you doing?

549
00:36:06,891 --> 00:36:08,685
We gotta go.
We gotta go now!

550
00:36:08,851 --> 00:36:11,688
No, no, just a little more
and we'll tie it off.

551
00:36:11,771 --> 00:36:13,523
(GROWLING)

552
00:36:15,358 --> 00:36:16,526
Minho, stay with me.
(YELPS)

553
00:36:17,110 --> 00:36:18,403
Stay with me, Minho.

554
00:36:18,569 --> 00:36:20,071
Just a little more,
we're almost there.

555
00:36:20,238 --> 00:36:21,739
I'm sorry, Greenie.
What?

556
00:36:21,906 --> 00:36:22,907
Minho! (YELPING)

557
00:36:26,077 --> 00:36:27,787
(DISTANT ROARING)
(WHIMPERS)

558
00:36:28,705 --> 00:36:30,331
(GRUNTING)

559
00:36:38,339 --> 00:36:40,299
(SCUTTLING)

560
00:36:42,176 --> 00:36:43,594
(ROARING)

561
00:36:59,736 --> 00:37:01,404
(GASPING)

562
00:37:03,114 --> 00:37:04,449
Okay.

563
00:37:16,961 --> 00:37:18,379
(GRUNTING)

564
00:37:21,758 --> 00:37:23,259
Come on.

565
00:37:24,969 --> 00:37:26,095
(PANTING)

566
00:37:31,100 --> 00:37:33,394
(CREATURE RETREATING)

567
00:37:49,619 --> 00:37:52,455
(WALLS SHIFTING)

568
00:37:52,622 --> 00:37:56,375
(DISTANT ROARING)

569
00:38:03,883 --> 00:38:05,468
(SQUISHES)

570
00:38:20,942 --> 00:38:22,360
Whoa!

571
00:38:32,620 --> 00:38:34,372
(SCREAMS)
(ROARS)

572
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:41,462
(PANTING)

573
00:38:49,679 --> 00:38:50,847
Oh!

574
00:38:52,515 --> 00:38:53,850
Oh, shit!

575
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:00,690
(SCREAMS)

576
00:39:03,150 --> 00:39:04,277
Whoa!

577
00:39:08,364 --> 00:39:09,365
(PANTING)

578
00:39:12,535 --> 00:39:13,619
Whoa!

579
00:39:13,703 --> 00:39:14,996
(ROARING)

580
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:29,176
(YELLS)

581
00:39:29,969 --> 00:39:31,304
(GRUNTING)

582
00:39:46,944 --> 00:39:48,738
(SCREAMING)

583
00:39:49,739 --> 00:39:51,032
(GROANS)

584
00:40:01,667 --> 00:40:02,668
(GASPS)

585
00:40:02,752 --> 00:40:04,670
You're a crazy
son of a bitch.

586
00:40:06,172 --> 00:40:08,049
Come on, follow me.
Come on!

587
00:40:10,092 --> 00:40:11,802
(BOTH PANTING)

588
00:40:11,886 --> 00:40:13,721
(WALLS SHIFTING)

589
00:40:14,096 --> 00:40:17,516
Okay, it's changing.
Come on, come on!

590
00:40:18,434 --> 00:40:19,769
This section
is closing.
Come on.

591
00:40:19,936 --> 00:40:21,604
We can lose
it down here!

592
00:40:28,444 --> 00:40:29,445
Thomas!

593
00:40:29,612 --> 00:40:31,113
What are you waiting for?
Get out of there!

594
00:40:35,409 --> 00:40:37,286
(ROARING)

595
00:40:38,079 --> 00:40:39,121
Come on!

596
00:40:43,626 --> 00:40:44,752
Come on!

597
00:40:44,919 --> 00:40:46,253
Come on, Thomas!
Don't look back!

598
00:40:46,963 --> 00:40:48,130
Run!
(SCREAMS)

599
00:40:48,589 --> 00:40:50,132
Move it, Thomas! Go on!

600
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:53,052
Move your ass!
Let's go! Come on!

601
00:40:53,219 --> 00:40:55,137
Come on, Greenie!
Let's go!

602
00:40:55,763 --> 00:40:57,098
Thomas!

603
00:41:04,939 --> 00:41:07,233
Guys, get up!

604
00:41:22,665 --> 00:41:24,417
I told you, Chuck.

605
00:41:24,583 --> 00:41:26,627
They're not coming back.

606
00:41:27,503 --> 00:41:28,963
BOY: Let's go.

607
00:41:38,180 --> 00:41:39,682
No way.

608
00:41:40,975 --> 00:41:41,976
Yeah!

609
00:41:42,977 --> 00:41:43,978
Yes!

610
00:41:44,603 --> 00:41:45,604
Yeah!

611
00:41:46,439 --> 00:41:48,566
(BOYS EXCLAIMING IN SURPRISE)

612
00:41:50,359 --> 00:41:51,652
I got him,
I got him, I got him.

613
00:41:51,819 --> 00:41:53,696
Watch out. Easy.

614
00:41:54,613 --> 00:41:56,490
What happened out there?
How did you guys make it out?

615
00:42:01,203 --> 00:42:02,288
You saw a Griever?

616
00:42:03,873 --> 00:42:05,708
Yeah, I saw one.

617
00:42:06,667 --> 00:42:08,377
He didn't just see it.

618
00:42:08,544 --> 00:42:10,546
He killed it.

619
00:42:17,553 --> 00:42:19,805
(BOYS CHATTERING EXCITEDLY)

620
00:42:21,557 --> 00:42:23,142
Things are changing.

621
00:42:23,601 --> 00:42:24,977
(BOYS SHUSHING)

622
00:42:25,061 --> 00:42:26,729
There's no denying that.

623
00:42:28,481 --> 00:42:31,484
First, Ben gets
stung in broad daylight.

624
00:42:32,151 --> 00:42:33,736
And then Alby.

625
00:42:34,862 --> 00:42:38,324
And now our Greenie, here,
has taken it upon himself...

626
00:42:38,491 --> 00:42:40,076
to go into the maze.

627
00:42:41,327 --> 00:42:44,580
Which is a
clear violation of
our rules here.

628
00:42:44,747 --> 00:42:47,583
Yeah...
but he saved Alby's life.

629
00:42:48,584 --> 00:42:49,877
Did he?

630
00:42:52,505 --> 00:42:55,925
For 3 years,
we have coexisted
with these things.

631
00:42:56,092 --> 00:42:58,094
And now, you've killed
one of them.

632
00:43:00,763 --> 00:43:03,182
Who knows what that
could mean for us.

633
00:43:04,016 --> 00:43:06,185
What do you
suggest we do?

634
00:43:06,936 --> 00:43:08,354
He has to
be punished.

635
00:43:08,437 --> 00:43:09,688
(BOYS PROTESTING)

636
00:43:09,772 --> 00:43:11,107
Come on.
He killed a Griever!

637
00:43:12,274 --> 00:43:13,275
Minho.

638
00:43:13,776 --> 00:43:16,237
You were there with him.
What do you think?

639
00:43:19,865 --> 00:43:21,617
I think...

640
00:43:21,784 --> 00:43:24,703
in all the time
we've been here...

641
00:43:24,870 --> 00:43:27,748
no one has ever
killed a Griever before.

642
00:43:31,544 --> 00:43:33,921
When I turned
tail and ran...

643
00:43:34,088 --> 00:43:37,383
this dumb shank stayed
behind to help Alby.

644
00:43:38,926 --> 00:43:41,887
Look, I don't know
if he's brave or stupid.

645
00:43:45,307 --> 00:43:47,601
But whatever it is,
we need more of it.

646
00:43:49,228 --> 00:43:50,479
I say we make
him a runner.

647
00:43:50,646 --> 00:43:52,731
FRY: A runner? What?
(BOYS CHATTERING)

648
00:43:53,315 --> 00:43:55,109
Minho, let's not
jump the gun, here.

649
00:43:55,276 --> 00:43:58,154
Thomas! Thomas! Thomas!

650
00:43:59,155 --> 00:44:02,283
If you want to throw
the newbie a parade,
that's fine.

651
00:44:02,449 --> 00:44:04,160
Go ahead.

652
00:44:04,285 --> 00:44:06,954
But if there is one thing
I know about the maze...

653
00:44:07,121 --> 00:44:08,330
it is that you do not...

654
00:44:19,175 --> 00:44:21,427
(BOYS SHOUTING)

655
00:44:23,512 --> 00:44:24,930
Okay, wait.
I know that sound.

656
00:44:25,097 --> 00:44:26,182
The Box.
It's coming back up.

657
00:44:26,265 --> 00:44:27,308
It shouldn't be.

658
00:44:32,062 --> 00:44:34,064
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

659
00:44:39,028 --> 00:44:40,029
FRY:
Newt, what do you see?

660
00:44:40,112 --> 00:44:41,530
BOY 1: Do you see it?

661
00:44:42,531 --> 00:44:43,532
It's a girl.

662
00:44:43,616 --> 00:44:45,826
(BOYS EXCLAIMING IN SURPRISE)

663
00:44:46,035 --> 00:44:47,036
BOY 2: No way.

664
00:44:51,040 --> 00:44:52,875
NEWT: I think she's dead.

665
00:44:53,709 --> 00:44:55,044
What's in her hand?

666
00:45:06,639 --> 00:45:11,185
"She's the
last one... ever."

667
00:45:14,647 --> 00:45:15,648
What the hell
does that mean?

668
00:45:15,731 --> 00:45:16,815
(GASPING)

669
00:45:16,899 --> 00:45:17,858
ALL: Whoa!

670
00:45:17,942 --> 00:45:18,943
(PANTING)

671
00:45:19,652 --> 00:45:21,195
Thomas...

672
00:45:36,919 --> 00:45:39,338
Do you still think
I'm overreacting?

673
00:45:51,558 --> 00:45:53,143
(ALBY BREATHING HEAVILY)

674
00:45:53,227 --> 00:45:55,688
NEWT:
Jeff, what's going on?

675
00:45:55,854 --> 00:45:57,898
What's the matter with her?
Why won't she wake up?

676
00:45:58,065 --> 00:46:01,068
Hey man, I got my job
the same way you did.

677
00:46:07,283 --> 00:46:08,867
Do you
recognize her?

678
00:46:09,785 --> 00:46:10,869
No.

679
00:46:11,287 --> 00:46:14,123
Really? Because
she seemed to
recognize you.

680
00:46:15,624 --> 00:46:16,792
What about
the note?

681
00:46:17,710 --> 00:46:20,129
We'll worry
about the note later.

682
00:46:20,296 --> 00:46:22,631
I think you should
worry about it now.

683
00:46:24,300 --> 00:46:26,427
We've got enough to
deal with at the moment.

684
00:46:26,593 --> 00:46:28,304
He's right, Newt.

685
00:46:29,263 --> 00:46:30,889
If the Box isn't
coming back up,

686
00:46:30,973 --> 00:46:32,474
how long do you
think we can last?

687
00:46:33,309 --> 00:46:35,144
No one said that.

688
00:46:35,728 --> 00:46:37,938
Let's not jump
to any conclusions.

689
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:41,400
We'll just wait
until she wakes up
and see what she knows.

690
00:46:43,485 --> 00:46:45,988
Somebody has gotta have
some answers around here.

691
00:46:47,781 --> 00:46:48,782
Okay.

692
00:46:50,242 --> 00:46:52,953
Where are you going?
Back into the maze.

693
00:46:57,833 --> 00:46:58,834
Hey.

694
00:46:59,793 --> 00:47:01,170
Hey, Thomas.

695
00:47:02,338 --> 00:47:05,424
What is this with you, huh?
A death wish?

696
00:47:05,591 --> 00:47:07,760
You just got out and
now you want back in?

697
00:47:07,843 --> 00:47:08,886
(SIGHS)

698
00:47:08,969 --> 00:47:10,929
Newt said that no one
has ever seen a Griever

699
00:47:11,013 --> 00:47:12,931
and lived to tell
about it, right?

700
00:47:13,098 --> 00:47:15,517
Minho, now we have one.

701
00:47:15,684 --> 00:47:18,687
You're telling me
you're not even
a little bit curious?

702
00:47:18,854 --> 00:47:20,481
Not really, no.

703
00:47:25,194 --> 00:47:26,695
So, what's the plan?

704
00:47:26,862 --> 00:47:28,781
You're gonna go out
and dissect that
thing all by yourself?

705
00:47:28,947 --> 00:47:30,699
I will if I have to.

706
00:47:31,492 --> 00:47:33,369
Have the other
runners left yet?

707
00:47:33,535 --> 00:47:35,704
The other runners
quit this morning.

708
00:47:38,040 --> 00:47:39,541
(SIGHS) After Alby
got stung, they're not

709
00:47:39,625 --> 00:47:41,210
in any hurry to
get back out there.

710
00:47:43,212 --> 00:47:45,047
Why are you?

711
00:47:46,715 --> 00:47:49,718
I think it's time
we find out what
we're really up against.

712
00:47:53,514 --> 00:47:54,848
All right.

713
00:47:55,015 --> 00:47:57,226
But you're not going
back out there alone.

714
00:47:57,393 --> 00:47:58,727
Meet me in the woods
in half-an-hour.

715
00:48:16,078 --> 00:48:17,246
(EXHALES)

716
00:48:22,334 --> 00:48:24,211
Will this be enough?

717
00:48:27,756 --> 00:48:29,091
Okay.

718
00:48:30,259 --> 00:48:31,760
Let's go.

719
00:48:48,360 --> 00:48:49,570
Come on!

720
00:49:11,800 --> 00:49:13,635
That's disgusting.

721
00:49:14,803 --> 00:49:16,472
There's something
in there.

722
00:49:17,306 --> 00:49:19,391
You mean, besides
a Griever pancake?

723
00:49:27,816 --> 00:49:30,068
Whoa, what are
you doing?

724
00:49:42,331 --> 00:49:43,499
ALL: Whoa!

725
00:49:45,125 --> 00:49:47,127
I thought you
said it was dead.

726
00:49:47,503 --> 00:49:48,712
Was it a reflex?

727
00:49:48,795 --> 00:49:49,963
You hope.

728
00:49:52,132 --> 00:49:54,259
Okay, come on.
Let's try and
pull it out.

729
00:49:55,010 --> 00:49:56,637
Everyone get
a hand on it.
Come on.

730
00:49:56,803 --> 00:49:58,514
All right, ready?
On three.

731
00:49:58,680 --> 00:50:00,474
One, two, three!

732
00:50:00,557 --> 00:50:02,559
(ALL GRUNTING)

733
00:50:06,438 --> 00:50:08,524
(ALL PANTING)

734
00:50:10,025 --> 00:50:11,735
Are you okay, Fry?
Yeah. Thanks, brother.

735
00:50:40,180 --> 00:50:41,557
(BOYS GROANING IN DISGUST)

736
00:50:46,770 --> 00:50:48,313
What the hell is that?

737
00:50:57,656 --> 00:50:58,657
Interesting.

738
00:50:58,824 --> 00:51:00,200
FRY:
Okay, whatever it is...

739
00:51:00,367 --> 00:51:02,244
can we take this up
back at the Glade?

740
00:51:02,369 --> 00:51:04,955
Because I don't
want to meet
this guy's friends.

741
00:51:05,247 --> 00:51:06,623
He's right.

742
00:51:06,790 --> 00:51:09,459
It's getting late.
Come on.

743
00:51:20,887 --> 00:51:21,888
THOMAS: We found this.

744
00:51:22,764 --> 00:51:24,975
It was inside a Griever.

745
00:51:25,142 --> 00:51:27,728
These are the same letters
we get in our supplies.
Yeah.

746
00:51:27,894 --> 00:51:31,273
Whoever put us
here obviously
made the Grievers.

747
00:51:31,440 --> 00:51:32,858
This is the
first real clue,

748
00:51:32,941 --> 00:51:34,610
the first anything,
you've found in
over 3 years.

749
00:51:34,776 --> 00:51:35,986
Right, Minho?

750
00:51:36,069 --> 00:51:37,279
Right.

751
00:51:37,654 --> 00:51:40,198
THOMAS: Newt, we gotta
go back out there.

752
00:51:40,532 --> 00:51:43,243
Who knows where
this might lead us.

753
00:51:45,704 --> 00:51:47,623
You see what he's
trying to do, right?

754
00:51:48,498 --> 00:51:49,791
First he breaks
our rules...

755
00:51:49,958 --> 00:51:52,586
and then he
tries to convince us
to abandon them totally.

756
00:51:53,086 --> 00:51:55,422
The rules are the only
thing that have ever
held us together.

757
00:51:55,631 --> 00:51:58,008
Why now are we
questioning that?

758
00:51:58,467 --> 00:52:00,761
If Alby was here,
you know he'd
agree with me.

759
00:52:00,927 --> 00:52:04,097
This shank needs
to be punished.

760
00:52:12,022 --> 00:52:13,148
You're right.

761
00:52:13,315 --> 00:52:15,025
Thomas broke the rules.

762
00:52:15,609 --> 00:52:16,943
One night in the pit,
and no food.

763
00:52:17,110 --> 00:52:19,821
Come on, Newt!
One night in the pit?

764
00:52:19,988 --> 00:52:22,282
Do you think
that's gonna stop him
from going into the maze?

765
00:52:22,449 --> 00:52:23,617
No.

766
00:52:23,784 --> 00:52:25,327
And we can't just
have non-runners

767
00:52:25,410 --> 00:52:27,412
running into the maze
whenever they feel like it.

768
00:52:29,331 --> 00:52:30,791
So let's just
make this official.

769
00:52:30,957 --> 00:52:33,335
Starting from tomorrow,
you're a runner.

770
00:52:38,507 --> 00:52:39,508
Wow.

771
00:52:39,966 --> 00:52:41,718
Gally...
No, Fry.

772
00:52:49,518 --> 00:52:50,769
Thanks, Newt.

773
00:53:08,495 --> 00:53:09,913
Hey, where
are we going?

774
00:53:10,080 --> 00:53:12,124
You'll see.

775
00:53:36,732 --> 00:53:37,858
(SIGHS)

776
00:53:39,401 --> 00:53:41,111
It's the maze.

777
00:53:42,320 --> 00:53:43,739
All of it.

778
00:53:45,741 --> 00:53:48,994
What do you mean "all of it"?
I thought you were
still mapping it.

779
00:53:50,203 --> 00:53:51,913
There's nothing
left to map.

780
00:53:54,249 --> 00:53:55,375
I've run every
inch of it myself.

781
00:53:56,418 --> 00:53:57,878
Every cycle.

782
00:53:58,044 --> 00:53:59,504
Every pattern.

783
00:54:01,673 --> 00:54:02,674
If there was
a way out,

784
00:54:02,758 --> 00:54:04,593
we would have
found it by now.

785
00:54:06,553 --> 00:54:08,889
Why haven't you
told anyone this?

786
00:54:10,849 --> 00:54:13,059
It was Alby's call.

787
00:54:13,226 --> 00:54:16,104
People needed to
believe we had a chance
of getting out.

788
00:54:17,814 --> 00:54:19,107
But maybe now...

789
00:54:20,484 --> 00:54:21,860
we have a real chance.

790
00:54:25,113 --> 00:54:26,448
(SIGHS)

791
00:54:27,324 --> 00:54:28,617
Take a look at this.

792
00:54:29,785 --> 00:54:32,496
About a year ago,
we started exploring
these outer sections.

793
00:54:32,746 --> 00:54:35,707
We found these numbers
printed on the walls.

794
00:54:35,874 --> 00:54:38,418
Sections 1 through 8.

795
00:54:38,668 --> 00:54:39,878
See, the way it works,

796
00:54:39,961 --> 00:54:42,380
is every night,
when the maze changes...

797
00:54:42,547 --> 00:54:44,424
it opens up
a new section.

798
00:54:44,591 --> 00:54:47,010
So today,
Section 6 was open.

799
00:54:47,177 --> 00:54:50,847
Tomorrow, it will be 4,
then 8, then 3.

800
00:54:51,014 --> 00:54:53,350
The pattern
always stays the same.

801
00:54:56,728 --> 00:54:58,563
What's so
special about 7?

802
00:54:58,730 --> 00:55:00,190
I don't know.

803
00:55:01,233 --> 00:55:03,151
But last night,
when you killed
that Griever...

804
00:55:03,944 --> 00:55:05,779
Section 7 was open.

805
00:55:05,946 --> 00:55:08,448
I think it must be
where it comes from.

806
00:55:08,615 --> 00:55:10,325
Tomorrow,
you and I are gonna
take a closer look.

807
00:55:12,577 --> 00:55:13,578
Hey!

808
00:55:13,870 --> 00:55:15,789
What are you guys doing?
You're not allowed in here.

809
00:55:15,956 --> 00:55:17,249
(PANTING)
Sorry, it's just
the, uh...

810
00:55:17,332 --> 00:55:18,542
It's the girl.

811
00:55:18,875 --> 00:55:20,168
Is she awake?

812
00:55:20,669 --> 00:55:21,670
You could
say that.

813
00:55:22,504 --> 00:55:24,339
Chuck,
what's going on?
(LAUGHING)

814
00:55:24,923 --> 00:55:27,175
Girls are awesome.
(BOYS CLAMORING)

815
00:55:27,259 --> 00:55:28,510
GIRL: Leave me alone!

816
00:55:28,677 --> 00:55:30,595
FRY: Watch your head!
(BOYS SHOUTING)

817
00:55:30,679 --> 00:55:33,265
Hey, throw one more
of those things... Ow!

818
00:55:33,348 --> 00:55:34,850
Go away!
We come in peace!

819
00:55:35,016 --> 00:55:36,017
What happened?
Just duck!

820
00:55:36,184 --> 00:55:37,602
I don't think she
likes us very much.

821
00:55:37,769 --> 00:55:39,521
GIRL: What do you
want from me?
We just wanna talk.

822
00:55:39,688 --> 00:55:40,856
I'm warning you!

823
00:55:41,022 --> 00:55:42,566
Take cover, y'all!
Take cover!

824
00:55:42,649 --> 00:55:43,775
(ALL SHOUTING)

825
00:55:43,859 --> 00:55:46,027
Hey, it's Thomas!
It's Thomas!

826
00:55:52,742 --> 00:55:54,870
I'm gonna
come up, okay?

827
00:55:58,582 --> 00:55:59,583
Okay.

828
00:56:00,709 --> 00:56:02,210
Just me.

829
00:56:06,381 --> 00:56:07,757
I'm coming up.

830
00:56:09,217 --> 00:56:10,552
(BOYS CHATTERING)

831
00:56:12,929 --> 00:56:14,598
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

832
00:56:15,599 --> 00:56:16,725
Okay, just...

833
00:56:16,892 --> 00:56:18,268
Easy, all right?

834
00:56:19,102 --> 00:56:20,562
Where am I?

835
00:56:20,729 --> 00:56:22,564
What is this place?

836
00:56:22,731 --> 00:56:24,065
Why can't
I remember
anything?

837
00:56:24,232 --> 00:56:26,985
This is all normal. Okay?
We've all been through this.

838
00:56:27,277 --> 00:56:28,278
Okay?

839
00:56:29,446 --> 00:56:31,406
Your name will
come back to you
in a couple of days.

840
00:56:31,573 --> 00:56:33,408
It's the one
thing that...
Teresa.

841
00:56:34,910 --> 00:56:35,911
What did you say?

842
00:56:36,077 --> 00:56:37,245
My name.

843
00:56:38,079 --> 00:56:39,915
It's Teresa.

844
00:56:41,583 --> 00:56:43,335
Teresa, I'm Thomas.

845
00:56:46,171 --> 00:56:49,299
But you already knew that,
though, I guess, huh?

846
00:56:50,508 --> 00:56:53,428
They said I kept saying
your name in my sleep.

847
00:56:53,595 --> 00:56:54,763
Who are you?

848
00:56:59,434 --> 00:57:00,644
I don't know.

849
00:57:03,271 --> 00:57:05,190
(STAMMERING)
I can't remember.

850
00:57:05,357 --> 00:57:08,360
None of us here can
remember anything.

851
00:57:09,611 --> 00:57:11,780
We all woke up here
just like you did.

852
00:57:13,114 --> 00:57:14,616
Hey, I promise...

853
00:57:17,953 --> 00:57:19,537
I'm gonna take this.

854
00:57:22,457 --> 00:57:23,625
Okay. (SIGHS)

855
00:57:25,043 --> 00:57:26,628
GALLY:
What's going on up there?

856
00:57:30,298 --> 00:57:31,967
Is she coming down?

857
00:57:32,801 --> 00:57:33,802
Um...

858
00:57:40,809 --> 00:57:43,311
Hey, listen, you guys just
give us a second, okay?

859
00:57:45,647 --> 00:57:46,731
All right.

860
00:57:47,399 --> 00:57:48,400
Come on.

861
00:57:48,858 --> 00:57:50,986
Is this what all
girls are like?

862
00:57:53,405 --> 00:57:55,073
ZART: That girl is crazy.

863
00:57:59,577 --> 00:58:02,706
"She's the last one."
What does that mean?

864
00:58:03,039 --> 00:58:04,499
I'm not sure.

865
00:58:06,167 --> 00:58:07,127
Ever since
you came up,

866
00:58:07,210 --> 00:58:08,878
that Box hasn't
gone back down.

867
00:58:10,755 --> 00:58:13,425
I just think
it's got everyone
a little worried.

868
00:58:15,510 --> 00:58:17,220
Especially Gally.

869
00:58:20,765 --> 00:58:22,684
He thinks
it's my fault.

870
00:58:27,355 --> 00:58:29,357
Are you sure you don't
remember anything else?

871
00:58:31,693 --> 00:58:33,111
I remember water...

872
00:58:34,237 --> 00:58:35,780
feeling like
I was drowning.

873
00:58:38,033 --> 00:58:40,035
These faces
staring at me.

874
00:58:42,704 --> 00:58:46,541
And this woman's voice
saying the same
thing over and over.

875
00:58:46,708 --> 00:58:47,917
"Wicked is good."

876
00:58:52,213 --> 00:58:54,924
Ever since I've been here,
I've had these dreams.

877
00:58:55,091 --> 00:58:57,218
Well, I thought
they were dreams.

878
00:59:00,263 --> 00:59:01,264
You...

879
00:59:02,557 --> 00:59:04,392
You were there.

880
00:59:06,978 --> 00:59:07,979
You were there...

881
00:59:08,146 --> 00:59:11,107
and you told me
that everything
was gonna change.

882
00:59:14,319 --> 00:59:16,071
What does it mean?

883
00:59:18,073 --> 00:59:21,242
I don't know.
I just always get pieces.

884
00:59:22,243 --> 00:59:24,579
And the others don't
remember anything?

885
00:59:24,746 --> 00:59:25,747
No.

886
00:59:28,792 --> 00:59:30,418
Why are we different?

887
00:59:38,176 --> 00:59:40,261
These were in my
pocket when I came up.

888
00:59:47,310 --> 00:59:49,687
"W.C. K. D."

889
00:59:52,649 --> 00:59:54,776
"Wicked is good."

890
00:59:56,569 --> 00:59:58,988
What if we were
sent here for a reason?

891
01:00:03,118 --> 01:00:04,077
Alby.

892
01:00:04,160 --> 01:00:05,245
(GROANING SOFTLY)

893
01:00:05,328 --> 01:00:07,247
NEWT: We don't even
know what this stuff is.

894
01:00:07,455 --> 01:00:08,957
We don't know
who sent it.

895
01:00:09,124 --> 01:00:10,792
Or why it came
up here with you.

896
01:00:10,959 --> 01:00:13,920
For all we know,
this thing
could kill him.

897
01:00:14,087 --> 01:00:15,588
He's already dying.

898
01:00:16,464 --> 01:00:17,632
Look at him.

899
01:00:18,633 --> 01:00:21,469
How could
this possibly make
it any worse?

900
01:00:21,553 --> 01:00:22,679
(CONTINUES GROANING)

901
01:00:22,762 --> 01:00:24,973
Come on,
it's worth a try.

902
01:00:28,476 --> 01:00:29,811
All right.

903
01:00:30,603 --> 01:00:31,813
Do it.

904
01:00:41,156 --> 01:00:42,282
Okay.

905
01:00:43,324 --> 01:00:44,367
(GASPS)

906
01:00:44,450 --> 01:00:46,327
You shouldn't be here!
You shouldn't be here!

907
01:00:46,494 --> 01:00:47,537
No!

908
01:00:48,121 --> 01:00:49,455
Watch out!

909
01:00:49,956 --> 01:00:51,916
(GRUNTING)

910
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:53,835
Get the syringe! Let go!

911
01:00:53,918 --> 01:00:54,919
(BOTH PANTING)

912
01:01:03,469 --> 01:01:05,346
Well, that worked.

913
01:01:05,805 --> 01:01:07,098
Okay, from now on...

914
01:01:07,265 --> 01:01:10,351
someone stays here
and watches him
around the clock.

915
01:01:14,856 --> 01:01:16,191
Hey.

916
01:01:19,110 --> 01:01:21,946
Sundown, Greenie.
Time to go.

917
01:01:37,837 --> 01:01:40,006
Hey, what is your
problem with me?

918
01:01:40,673 --> 01:01:43,509
Everything started
going wrong the minute
you showed up.

919
01:01:44,219 --> 01:01:46,387
First Ben, then Alby...

920
01:01:47,180 --> 01:01:48,514
and now the girl.

921
01:01:50,225 --> 01:01:52,143
Everybody saw
she recognized you.

922
01:01:54,145 --> 01:01:56,731
And I'm betting
you know who she is.

923
01:02:03,112 --> 01:02:04,405
(SIGHS)

924
01:02:12,080 --> 01:02:13,206
Gally...

925
01:02:15,792 --> 01:02:18,878
you know we can't
stay here forever,
right?

926
01:02:37,355 --> 01:02:38,940
(RUSTLING)

927
01:02:39,399 --> 01:02:40,400
Who's there?

928
01:02:41,651 --> 01:02:42,652
It's just me.

929
01:02:43,528 --> 01:02:44,779
Sorry, Chuck.

930
01:02:44,946 --> 01:02:46,239
Here.

931
01:02:46,406 --> 01:02:48,574
You'll run better
on a full stomach.

932
01:02:58,626 --> 01:03:00,169
Mmm...

933
01:03:01,337 --> 01:03:02,547
Thanks, Chuck.

934
01:03:07,760 --> 01:03:09,429
Hey, what do
you got there?

935
01:03:15,518 --> 01:03:18,146
Wow, that came out
pretty damn good.

936
01:03:18,479 --> 01:03:19,647
What's that for?

937
01:03:21,190 --> 01:03:23,109
It's for my parents.

938
01:03:23,776 --> 01:03:25,862
You remember
your parents?

939
01:03:26,738 --> 01:03:28,114
No.

940
01:03:29,115 --> 01:03:31,117
I mean, I know
I must have them.

941
01:03:31,993 --> 01:03:33,036
(SIGHS)

942
01:03:33,119 --> 01:03:35,121
And wherever they are,
I'm sure they miss me...

943
01:03:35,747 --> 01:03:38,666
but I can't miss
them because I don't
remember them.

944
01:03:44,297 --> 01:03:47,508
What do you think
you're gonna find
out there tomorrow?

945
01:03:49,927 --> 01:03:51,346
Uh, I don't know.

946
01:03:53,848 --> 01:03:55,308
But if there's
a way out, Chuck,

947
01:03:55,391 --> 01:03:57,185
me and Minho
are gonna find it.

948
01:04:00,480 --> 01:04:01,564
(SIGHS)

949
01:04:03,524 --> 01:04:04,692
Here.

950
01:04:10,656 --> 01:04:12,533
Chuck, why would
you give this to me?

951
01:04:15,161 --> 01:04:17,038
I can't remember
them anyway.

952
01:04:18,873 --> 01:04:20,333
But maybe if you
find a way out,

953
01:04:20,416 --> 01:04:22,043
you can give it
to them for me.

954
01:04:24,879 --> 01:04:26,506
I'll let you
get some sleep.

955
01:04:36,224 --> 01:04:37,433
Hey, Chuck.

956
01:04:38,226 --> 01:04:39,227
Come here.

957
01:04:43,731 --> 01:04:45,274
Put out your hand.

958
01:04:47,402 --> 01:04:49,570
I want you to give
that to them yourself.

959
01:04:51,697 --> 01:04:53,074
We're gonna
get out of here.

960
01:04:53,408 --> 01:04:54,575
All of us.

961
01:04:55,868 --> 01:04:56,911
Okay?

962
01:04:57,578 --> 01:04:59,080
I promise.

963
01:05:01,457 --> 01:05:02,917
Yeah.
All right.

964
01:05:04,544 --> 01:05:06,629
Good night.
Good night, buddy.

965
01:05:19,934 --> 01:05:21,227
(SIGHS)

966
01:05:22,103 --> 01:05:23,563
Big day, Greenie.

967
01:05:23,646 --> 01:05:25,231
Are you sure
you don't wanna
sit this one out?

968
01:05:25,982 --> 01:05:28,443
Come on, man.
Get me out of here.
All right.

969
01:05:37,118 --> 01:05:39,662
(DOOR OPENING)

970
01:05:47,044 --> 01:05:48,045
Let's go!

971
01:05:53,092 --> 01:05:54,760
(PANTING)

972
01:06:00,016 --> 01:06:01,976
This way.
Not much further to
the inner ring.

973
01:06:02,143 --> 01:06:03,478
Let's go!

974
01:06:06,731 --> 01:06:07,899
Come on! This way.

975
01:06:26,250 --> 01:06:27,752
(BOTH PANTING)

976
01:06:34,133 --> 01:06:35,843
MINHO: That's strange.

977
01:06:35,968 --> 01:06:36,969
THOMAS: What?

978
01:06:37,136 --> 01:06:39,347
Seven is not
supposed to be open
for another week.

979
01:06:46,729 --> 01:06:49,482
THOMAS: What the
hell is this place?

980
01:06:49,649 --> 01:06:51,275
MINHO:
We call them blades.

981
01:07:10,294 --> 01:07:12,255
It's Ben's, isn't it?

982
01:07:12,421 --> 01:07:13,839
Yeah.

983
01:07:14,966 --> 01:07:17,218
A Griever must have
pulled him down here.

984
01:07:18,219 --> 01:07:20,346
(DEVICE POWERING UP)

985
01:07:24,225 --> 01:07:25,560
Whoa, hey!

986
01:07:27,562 --> 01:07:29,564
(DEVICE CLICKING)

987
01:07:41,826 --> 01:07:44,412
(DEVICE BEEPING)

988
01:07:47,623 --> 01:07:49,458
I think it's
showing us the way.

989
01:07:56,299 --> 01:07:58,676
Wait, wait, wait.
What, what?

990
01:07:59,260 --> 01:08:00,845
(BEEPING RAPIDLY)

991
01:08:00,928 --> 01:08:02,805
This way. Come on.

992
01:08:19,405 --> 01:08:22,408
(BEEPING INTENSIFIES)

993
01:08:26,370 --> 01:08:29,123
Minho, you ever see
this place before?

994
01:08:30,625 --> 01:08:31,959
No.

995
01:08:42,678 --> 01:08:45,598
(BEEPING ACCELERATES)

996
01:08:52,438 --> 01:08:53,439
(EXCLAIMS)

997
01:08:53,522 --> 01:08:55,483
It's just another
dead end.

998
01:09:00,446 --> 01:09:02,323
(DOOR OPENING)

999
01:09:23,010 --> 01:09:24,595
Are you sure
about this?

1000
01:09:28,182 --> 01:09:29,392
Nope.

1001
01:10:03,384 --> 01:10:04,885
Grievers.

1002
01:10:06,345 --> 01:10:07,888
(BUZZING)

1003
01:10:08,305 --> 01:10:09,390
(BEEPING)

1004
01:10:16,897 --> 01:10:18,399
What the
hell was that?

1005
01:10:20,192 --> 01:10:22,236
(ALARM BLARING)

1006
01:10:24,238 --> 01:10:25,906
We gotta
get out of here.

1007
01:10:26,073 --> 01:10:27,908
Give me the key,
give me the key!

1008
01:10:32,538 --> 01:10:33,539
(GASPS)

1009
01:10:33,622 --> 01:10:34,832
Move, move!

1010
01:10:37,668 --> 01:10:39,086
(BOTH PANTING)

1011
01:10:41,547 --> 01:10:43,257
We gotta go!
Run, Thomas!

1012
01:10:43,424 --> 01:10:45,050
We're gonna
get trapped!

1013
01:10:45,217 --> 01:10:46,427
Go! Go!

1014
01:10:46,802 --> 01:10:48,262
(YELLING)

1015
01:10:50,890 --> 01:10:52,057
MINHO: Go, go, go!
(CONTINUES YELLING)

1016
01:10:52,224 --> 01:10:53,225
Move!

1017
01:10:57,688 --> 01:10:59,064
(SHOUTS)

1018
01:11:01,942 --> 01:11:03,194
(BOTH PANTING HEAVILY)

1019
01:11:03,277 --> 01:11:04,278
Minho!

1020
01:11:04,445 --> 01:11:05,946
MINHO: Come on!
Let's go, let's go!

1021
01:11:09,283 --> 01:11:10,826
(BOTH YELLING)

1022
01:11:10,910 --> 01:11:11,911
Come on, move!

1023
01:11:12,077 --> 01:11:14,079
Keep going!
Keep going! Let's go!

1024
01:11:14,288 --> 01:11:15,748
BOTH: Whoa!

1025
01:11:16,081 --> 01:11:17,458
Go, go, go!

1026
01:11:18,375 --> 01:11:20,503
(BOTH PANTING HEAVILY)

1027
01:11:22,922 --> 01:11:23,923
Oh!

1028
01:11:32,807 --> 01:11:33,849
Go, go, go!

1029
01:11:39,355 --> 01:11:40,731
BOTH: Whoa!

1030
01:11:41,774 --> 01:11:43,442
Come on!
Don't look back!

1031
01:11:48,322 --> 01:11:49,573
Come on!

1032
01:11:49,657 --> 01:11:50,658
(THOMAS YELLS)

1033
01:11:52,201 --> 01:11:53,828
Oh, shit!

1034
01:11:55,329 --> 01:11:56,497
There!
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1035
01:12:01,961 --> 01:12:03,754
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1036
01:12:04,839 --> 01:12:06,090
(GROANING)

1037
01:12:12,513 --> 01:12:13,514
Oh!

1038
01:12:17,184 --> 01:12:18,561
NEWT: What the hell's
going on out there?

1039
01:12:18,727 --> 01:12:19,979
What the hell you
done now, Thomas?

1040
01:12:20,145 --> 01:12:21,605
We found something,
a new passage.

1041
01:12:21,689 --> 01:12:22,898
We think it
could be a way out.

1042
01:12:23,065 --> 01:12:24,817
Really?
It's true.

1043
01:12:24,984 --> 01:12:27,403
We opened a door,
something I'd
never seen before.

1044
01:12:27,570 --> 01:12:29,196
I think it must be
where the Grievers
go during the day.

1045
01:12:29,363 --> 01:12:30,531
Wait! Whoa, whoa, whoa...

1046
01:12:30,698 --> 01:12:32,867
You're saying you found
the Grievers' home?

1047
01:12:33,033 --> 01:12:34,201
And you want
us to go in?

1048
01:12:34,368 --> 01:12:35,870
Their way in could
be our way out, Chuck.

1049
01:12:36,036 --> 01:12:38,372
Yeah, or there could
be a dozen Grievers
on the other side.

1050
01:12:38,539 --> 01:12:41,750
The truth is,
Thomas doesn't know
what he has done, as usual.

1051
01:12:41,917 --> 01:12:43,627
Yeah, at least
I did something,
Gally.

1052
01:12:43,711 --> 01:12:44,879
I mean, what
have you done?

1053
01:12:45,045 --> 01:12:47,047
Aside from hide
behind these walls
all the time?

1054
01:12:47,214 --> 01:12:48,507
Let me tell you
something, Greenie.

1055
01:12:48,674 --> 01:12:51,260
You've been here
3 days, all right?
I've been here 3 years!

1056
01:12:51,427 --> 01:12:53,596
Yeah, you've been
here 3 years and you're
still here, Gally!

1057
01:12:53,762 --> 01:12:54,847
What does
that tell you?

1058
01:12:55,014 --> 01:12:56,515
Maybe you should
start doing things
a little differently.

1059
01:12:56,599 --> 01:12:58,726
Maybe you should
be in charge,
what about that?

1060
01:12:58,893 --> 01:13:00,728
Hey, it's Alby!

1061
01:13:01,228 --> 01:13:03,230
He's awake.

1062
01:13:04,398 --> 01:13:05,566
Has he said anything?

1063
01:13:05,733 --> 01:13:06,901
No.

1064
01:13:08,527 --> 01:13:10,070
Alby...

1065
01:13:13,532 --> 01:13:15,284
Alby, are you all right?

1066
01:13:21,540 --> 01:13:23,667
Hey, Alby.

1067
01:13:26,337 --> 01:13:29,048
Alby, we might
have just found a way
out of the maze.

1068
01:13:30,090 --> 01:13:33,010
Do you hear me?
We could be
getting out of here.

1069
01:13:35,054 --> 01:13:36,972
We can't.

1070
01:13:38,807 --> 01:13:40,392
We can't leave.

1071
01:13:41,602 --> 01:13:43,604
They won't let us.

1072
01:13:43,771 --> 01:13:45,189
What are you
talking about?

1073
01:13:46,190 --> 01:13:47,441
I remember.

1074
01:13:51,445 --> 01:13:53,530
What do
you remember?

1075
01:13:55,240 --> 01:13:56,700
You.

1076
01:14:01,080 --> 01:14:03,165
You were always
their favorite, Thomas.

1077
01:14:03,958 --> 01:14:05,209
Always.

1078
01:14:05,292 --> 01:14:08,295
(BOYS SHOUTING)

1079
01:14:09,338 --> 01:14:10,673
Why did you do this?

1080
01:14:11,882 --> 01:14:14,218
Why did you come here?

1081
01:14:14,301 --> 01:14:16,095
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

1082
01:14:16,178 --> 01:14:17,972
(CRYING)

1083
01:14:24,812 --> 01:14:25,813
Winston,
what's going on?

1084
01:14:25,980 --> 01:14:28,065
It's the doors.
They aren't closing.

1085
01:14:32,653 --> 01:14:35,656
(BOYS SHOUTING)

1086
01:14:53,507 --> 01:14:55,551
(LOUD CLANG)
(ALL GROAN)

1087
01:15:03,684 --> 01:15:05,310
(LOUD CLANG)
(BOYS SHOUTING)

1088
01:15:21,035 --> 01:15:23,412
Chuck, go to
the Council Hall

1089
01:15:23,537 --> 01:15:25,122
and start barricading
the doors.
Mmm-hmm.

1090
01:15:25,289 --> 01:15:27,041
Winston,
you go with him.
Got it.

1091
01:15:27,207 --> 01:15:29,626
Get the others.
Tell them to go to the forest.
Go hide, now!

1092
01:15:30,044 --> 01:15:32,171
Minho, I want you to grab
every weapon you can find.

1093
01:15:32,337 --> 01:15:34,465
I'll meet you
at Council Hall.
Let's go.

1094
01:15:35,257 --> 01:15:39,136
Teresa, you and I
are gonna go get Alby,
all right? Come on.

1095
01:15:39,219 --> 01:15:41,221
(BOYS SHOUTING
IN THE DISTANCE)

1096
01:15:42,056 --> 01:15:43,390
(ROARING)

1097
01:15:46,435 --> 01:15:48,479
All right, everybody hide!

1098
01:15:48,854 --> 01:15:49,855
Teresa!

1099
01:15:50,022 --> 01:15:53,025
Come on! Run! Run!

1100
01:15:58,238 --> 01:15:59,907
(BOYS SCREAMING
IN THE DISTANCE)

1101
01:16:01,283 --> 01:16:02,284
Stay down!

1102
01:16:02,701 --> 01:16:03,786
BOY 1: Run!

1103
01:16:08,999 --> 01:16:11,126
(GRIEVER GROWLING)
(BOY 2 SCREAMS)

1104
01:16:11,960 --> 01:16:13,670
(GRIEVER GROWLING)
(BOY 3 SCREAMS)

1105
01:16:13,754 --> 01:16:15,506
(BOYS SCREAMING IN DISTANCE)

1106
01:16:17,758 --> 01:16:19,093
Ahh!
Zart!

1107
01:16:19,176 --> 01:16:20,552
(SCREAMING)

1108
01:16:23,180 --> 01:16:26,225
ZART: Help me!
Go! Get to the village!

1109
01:16:33,148 --> 01:16:34,691
Go, go, go!

1110
01:16:34,775 --> 01:16:36,777
(ZART CONTINUES SCREAMING)

1111
01:16:40,114 --> 01:16:41,156
(SHUSHING)

1112
01:16:41,240 --> 01:16:42,866
Stay down,
stay down!

1113
01:16:43,283 --> 01:16:45,828
Gally! Let me in,
let me in!

1114
01:16:46,161 --> 01:16:47,454
(SCREAMS)

1115
01:16:52,626 --> 01:16:54,294
THOMAS: Alby!
TERESA: Are you okay?

1116
01:16:54,461 --> 01:16:55,462
What's going on?

1117
01:16:56,046 --> 01:16:58,173
They're here.
Grievers?

1118
01:16:58,257 --> 01:16:59,258
(BOY SCREAMING)

1119
01:17:04,638 --> 01:17:06,098
Thomas,
what do we do?

1120
01:17:06,265 --> 01:17:08,642
It's got me!
(SCREAMING)

1121
01:17:10,060 --> 01:17:11,687
(GRIEVER SNARLING)

1122
01:17:13,438 --> 01:17:14,731
Everybody, run, run, run!

1123
01:17:14,898 --> 01:17:16,316
Jeff, come on, go, go, go!

1124
01:17:19,444 --> 01:17:20,946
(ALL SHOUTING)

1125
01:17:27,119 --> 01:17:28,120
(YELLS)

1126
01:17:28,787 --> 01:17:30,330
(SCREECHING)

1127
01:17:31,707 --> 01:17:33,876
Everyone,
go, go, go!

1128
01:17:49,016 --> 01:17:50,350
(SCREAMS)

1129
01:17:50,893 --> 01:17:53,270
Keep moving!
Oh, shit!

1130
01:17:53,395 --> 01:17:54,563
Ahh!

1131
01:17:54,646 --> 01:17:56,023
JEFF: Alby!

1132
01:17:56,440 --> 01:17:57,649
Get behind me!

1133
01:18:00,861 --> 01:18:02,487
Come on!

1134
01:18:05,532 --> 01:18:06,825
FRY:
Over here, let's go!

1135
01:18:06,992 --> 01:18:09,578
Over here!
Let's go! Come on!

1136
01:18:11,872 --> 01:18:13,081
Over here, come on!

1137
01:18:13,248 --> 01:18:14,625
Winston!

1138
01:18:14,791 --> 01:18:15,959
Get Alby inside.

1139
01:18:16,919 --> 01:18:18,462
Chuck, get in! Go, go, go!

1140
01:18:20,505 --> 01:18:22,299
Lock down the doors!

1141
01:18:22,382 --> 01:18:24,009
(GRIEVER GROWLING)

1142
01:18:25,552 --> 01:18:28,889
(POUNDING ON DOOR)

1143
01:18:38,482 --> 01:18:40,275
TERESA: Careful.
(GRIEVER SNARLING)

1144
01:18:40,359 --> 01:18:41,735
ALL: Whoa!

1145
01:18:42,819 --> 01:18:44,071
NEWT: Stay back, guys.

1146
01:18:48,075 --> 01:18:50,077
(GRIEVER SCUTTLING ON ROOF)

1147
01:18:51,495 --> 01:18:52,621
(TERESA SHUSHING)

1148
01:19:00,420 --> 01:19:01,421
(ALL SCREAMING)

1149
01:19:04,007 --> 01:19:05,342
(ALL SCREAMING)

1150
01:19:06,468 --> 01:19:08,470
(ALL GROANING)

1151
01:19:09,221 --> 01:19:10,347
(ALL COUGHING)

1152
01:19:10,430 --> 01:19:11,515
NEWT: Is everyone all right?

1153
01:19:12,599 --> 01:19:14,351
BOY: Help!

1154
01:19:14,518 --> 01:19:16,270
Hey, grab him!
Help!

1155
01:19:18,021 --> 01:19:19,189
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

1156
01:19:19,273 --> 01:19:20,482
Watch out!

1157
01:19:21,233 --> 01:19:22,609
(GRIEVER GROWLING)

1158
01:19:25,612 --> 01:19:27,072
(ALL SCREAMING)

1159
01:19:27,155 --> 01:19:28,156
JEFF: Chuck!

1160
01:19:29,491 --> 01:19:30,784
(SCREAMS)

1161
01:19:30,867 --> 01:19:32,452
Chuck, no!
THOMAS: Grab him!

1162
01:19:32,619 --> 01:19:33,704
Pull him back!

1163
01:19:33,787 --> 01:19:35,038
(ALL GRUNTING)

1164
01:19:35,122 --> 01:19:36,707
CHUCK: Help!
Chuck, don't let go!

1165
01:19:36,873 --> 01:19:38,458
No shit!

1166
01:19:38,709 --> 01:19:40,502
TERESA: Pull!
NEWT: Don't let him go!

1167
01:19:40,585 --> 01:19:42,170
(ALL GRUNTING)

1168
01:19:44,965 --> 01:19:46,300
(YELLING)

1169
01:19:58,520 --> 01:19:59,813
(CONTINUES YELLING)

1170
01:20:00,105 --> 01:20:01,648
(CHUCK COUGHING)

1171
01:20:01,732 --> 01:20:03,150
Chuck, are you okay?
Yeah, I'm fine.

1172
01:20:05,819 --> 01:20:06,862
Thanks, Alby.

1173
01:20:08,405 --> 01:20:09,781
Alby! Watch out!
(GROANS)

1174
01:20:10,824 --> 01:20:11,867
(ALL SHOUTING)

1175
01:20:12,034 --> 01:20:13,035
NEWT: Grab him!

1176
01:20:13,160 --> 01:20:14,161
(GRUNTING)

1177
01:20:16,747 --> 01:20:18,832
Thomas, get them out.

1178
01:20:21,001 --> 01:20:22,044
(SCREAMS)
Alby!

1179
01:20:22,210 --> 01:20:24,838
No!
TERESA: Thomas...

1180
01:20:25,005 --> 01:20:26,548
Thomas!
CHUCK: Don't go out there!

1181
01:20:26,715 --> 01:20:27,758
MINHO: No, Thomas, wait!

1182
01:20:28,091 --> 01:20:29,551
Thomas, wait!

1183
01:20:31,261 --> 01:20:32,679
(GRIEVERS ROARING
IN THE DISTANCE)

1184
01:20:32,971 --> 01:20:33,972
(BOYS SCREAMING
IN THE DISTANCE)

1185
01:20:37,851 --> 01:20:39,394
BOY: Where is everybody?

1186
01:20:39,561 --> 01:20:41,271
Who's that over there?

1187
01:20:48,278 --> 01:20:50,238
Gally... (GROANS)
(ALL PROTESTING)

1188
01:20:51,198 --> 01:20:53,742
This is all you, Thomas!
Look around!

1189
01:20:53,909 --> 01:20:55,535
MINHO: Back off, Gally!
It's not Thomas' fault!

1190
01:20:55,660 --> 01:20:56,620
GALLY: You heard
what Alby said!

1191
01:20:56,703 --> 01:20:57,954
He's one of them!
NEWT: One of who?

1192
01:20:58,121 --> 01:20:59,998
He's one of them,
and they sent him here

1193
01:21:00,082 --> 01:21:01,958
to destroy everything,
and now he has!

1194
01:21:02,376 --> 01:21:04,878
Look around, Thomas!
Look around!

1195
01:21:05,045 --> 01:21:06,046
This is your fault!

1196
01:21:06,213 --> 01:21:07,881
MINHO: Back off, Gally!
This is not Thomas' fault!

1197
01:21:08,048 --> 01:21:10,759
NEWT: What are you
talking about?
Calm down.

1198
01:21:12,636 --> 01:21:13,637
GALLY: They sent him here,

1199
01:21:13,720 --> 01:21:14,971
and now he's destroyed
everything that we've built!

1200
01:21:15,055 --> 01:21:16,556
NEWT: What are you
talking about?

1201
01:21:16,681 --> 01:21:18,183
(BOYS ARGUING)

1202
01:21:18,558 --> 01:21:20,227
Maybe he's right.

1203
01:21:20,394 --> 01:21:22,145
Thomas...

1204
01:21:23,271 --> 01:21:25,649
THOMAS: I need
to remember, Teresa.

1205
01:21:25,982 --> 01:21:27,567
Thomas...

1206
01:21:27,734 --> 01:21:29,778
Thomas!
No, don't!

1207
01:21:30,195 --> 01:21:32,447
(GROANING)
Thomas!

1208
01:21:32,614 --> 01:21:33,907
Chuck, get
the other syringe!

1209
01:21:34,950 --> 01:21:36,576
It's okay.

1210
01:21:36,743 --> 01:21:38,453
Thomas, I'm here.

1211
01:21:49,506 --> 01:21:50,590
THOMAS: <i>Who put us here?</i>

1212
01:21:52,426 --> 01:21:53,635
ALBY: <i>That we don't know.</i>

1213
01:21:58,974 --> 01:22:00,142
THOMAS: <i>Teresa...</i>

1214
01:22:00,308 --> 01:22:02,018
<i>why are we doing this?</i>

1215
01:22:05,856 --> 01:22:07,107
WOMAN: <i>Excellent, Thomas.</i>

1216
01:22:07,274 --> 01:22:08,316
Come with me.

1217
01:22:09,943 --> 01:22:11,862
Wicked isn't good.
WOMAN: <i>Thomas...</i>

1218
01:22:12,112 --> 01:22:13,530
Wicked is good.

1219
01:22:14,823 --> 01:22:15,866
THOMAS: <i>How could</i>
<i>this be my fault?</i>

1220
01:22:15,949 --> 01:22:17,117
BEN: <i>You did this!</i>

1221
01:22:17,617 --> 01:22:18,952
<i>I saw you!</i>

1222
01:22:20,787 --> 01:22:23,123
THOMAS: <i>I can't keep</i>
<i>watching them die.</i>

1223
01:22:29,129 --> 01:22:30,630
TERESA: Hey.

1224
01:22:31,965 --> 01:22:33,633
Are you okay?

1225
01:22:36,052 --> 01:22:37,804
What the hell
were you thinking?

1226
01:22:43,477 --> 01:22:44,644
What happened?

1227
01:22:45,353 --> 01:22:46,813
NEWT: Gally
has taken control.

1228
01:22:47,898 --> 01:22:50,859
He said we had a choice.
Either join him...

1229
01:22:51,026 --> 01:22:53,695
or get banished
at sundown with you.

1230
01:22:54,946 --> 01:22:57,324
(GROANS) And the others
agreed to that?

1231
01:22:58,366 --> 01:23:00,035
Gally has everyone
convinced that

1232
01:23:00,118 --> 01:23:02,204
you're the reason
all this has happened.

1233
01:23:04,998 --> 01:23:07,334
Well, he's been
right so far.

1234
01:23:08,919 --> 01:23:10,504
What are you
talking about?

1235
01:23:11,421 --> 01:23:13,173
This place...

1236
01:23:14,007 --> 01:23:16,343
it's not what
we thought it was.

1237
01:23:17,928 --> 01:23:20,347
It's not a prison,
it's a test.

1238
01:23:21,181 --> 01:23:23,183
It all started
when we were kids.

1239
01:23:24,267 --> 01:23:27,062
They would give us
these challenges.

1240
01:23:27,687 --> 01:23:30,232
They were experimenting
on us.

1241
01:23:31,358 --> 01:23:34,402
And then people
started disappearing.

1242
01:23:34,569 --> 01:23:37,364
Every month,
one after the other,
like clockwork.

1243
01:23:37,697 --> 01:23:39,616
They were sending
them up into the maze.

1244
01:23:40,242 --> 01:23:42,452
Yeah, but not all of us.

1245
01:23:43,036 --> 01:23:44,788
What do you mean?

1246
01:23:48,041 --> 01:23:49,709
Guys, I'm one of them.

1247
01:23:52,212 --> 01:23:54,756
The people
who put you here,
I worked with them.

1248
01:23:56,550 --> 01:23:59,302
I watched
you guys for years.

1249
01:23:59,803 --> 01:24:02,556
The entire time
you have been here...

1250
01:24:02,722 --> 01:24:04,724
I was on the other
side of it.

1251
01:24:07,561 --> 01:24:08,895
So were you.

1252
01:24:10,772 --> 01:24:11,940
What?

1253
01:24:13,567 --> 01:24:15,902
Teresa, we did this
to them.

1254
01:24:17,904 --> 01:24:19,114
No.

1255
01:24:20,407 --> 01:24:21,908
That can't be true.

1256
01:24:22,158 --> 01:24:25,495
THOMAS: It is. I saw it.

1257
01:24:27,247 --> 01:24:29,416
Why would they send us
up if we were with them?

1258
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:31,585
It doesn't matter.

1259
01:24:32,961 --> 01:24:34,421
NEWT: He's right.

1260
01:24:37,090 --> 01:24:38,758
It doesn't matter.

1261
01:24:39,509 --> 01:24:41,261
Any of it.

1262
01:24:42,429 --> 01:24:46,433
Because the people
we were before the maze
don't even exist anymore.

1263
01:24:46,600 --> 01:24:48,643
These Creators
took care of that.

1264
01:24:49,853 --> 01:24:53,481
But what does matter
is who we are now,
and what we do...

1265
01:24:53,648 --> 01:24:55,317
right now.

1266
01:24:56,359 --> 01:24:58,987
You went into the maze
and you found a way out.

1267
01:24:59,321 --> 01:25:02,449
Yeah, but if I hadn't,
Alby would still be alive.

1268
01:25:05,869 --> 01:25:07,329
Maybe.

1269
01:25:10,957 --> 01:25:12,459
But I know that
if he were here,

1270
01:25:12,542 --> 01:25:15,837
he would be telling you
the exact same thing.

1271
01:25:16,963 --> 01:25:20,216
Pick your ass up
and finish what you started.

1272
01:25:22,385 --> 01:25:23,678
Because if we do nothing...

1273
01:25:23,845 --> 01:25:26,973
then that means
Alby died for nothing,
and I can't have that.

1274
01:25:31,519 --> 01:25:33,021
Okay.

1275
01:25:34,814 --> 01:25:38,109
Okay, but we gotta
get through Gally first.

1276
01:26:07,180 --> 01:26:09,099
This is such a waste.

1277
01:26:14,854 --> 01:26:16,064
Gally...

1278
01:26:20,902 --> 01:26:22,862
It doesn't feel
right, man.

1279
01:26:24,030 --> 01:26:26,449
JEFF: Yeah, what if
Thomas is right?

1280
01:26:27,283 --> 01:26:29,369
Maybe he can
lead us home.

1281
01:26:31,579 --> 01:26:33,581
We are home.

1282
01:26:34,207 --> 01:26:35,875
Okay?

1283
01:26:37,127 --> 01:26:40,088
I don't wanna
have to cross any more
names off that wall.

1284
01:26:40,255 --> 01:26:41,589
You really think
banishing us

1285
01:26:41,673 --> 01:26:43,925
is gonna solve
anything?

1286
01:26:44,676 --> 01:26:46,052
No.

1287
01:26:47,220 --> 01:26:49,222
But this isn't
a banishing.

1288
01:26:50,181 --> 01:26:51,224
It's an offering.

1289
01:26:51,391 --> 01:26:53,226
What? Wait!

1290
01:26:53,309 --> 01:26:55,353
Gally, what are you doing?

1291
01:26:55,520 --> 01:26:57,313
You really think
I'm gonna let Thomas

1292
01:26:57,397 --> 01:26:59,190
back into the maze
after what he has done?

1293
01:27:00,942 --> 01:27:02,610
Look around you!

1294
01:27:03,903 --> 01:27:05,029
Look at our Glade!

1295
01:27:06,614 --> 01:27:09,576
This is the only way.

1296
01:27:09,743 --> 01:27:13,037
And when the Grievers get
what they came here for...

1297
01:27:13,621 --> 01:27:15,749
everything goes back
to the way it was.

1298
01:27:15,915 --> 01:27:17,125
Are you listening
to this?

1299
01:27:17,292 --> 01:27:19,794
Why are you all
just standing there?
He's crazy!

1300
01:27:19,878 --> 01:27:21,838
You shut up.
If you stay here,

1301
01:27:21,921 --> 01:27:23,131
the Grievers are
going to come back.

1302
01:27:23,339 --> 01:27:25,258
They're gonna come back,
and they're gonna
keep coming back...

1303
01:27:25,425 --> 01:27:26,593
until you're all dead!

1304
01:27:26,760 --> 01:27:28,595
Shut up! Tie him up!

1305
01:27:30,263 --> 01:27:32,265
Do you hear me?
I said tie him up!

1306
01:27:35,852 --> 01:27:37,687
(ALL GRUNTING)

1307
01:27:57,290 --> 01:27:58,917
You're full of surprises,
aren't you?

1308
01:27:59,292 --> 01:28:02,295
You don't have
to come with us,
but we are leaving.

1309
01:28:02,462 --> 01:28:04,756
Anyone else who
wants to come,
now is your last chance.

1310
01:28:04,923 --> 01:28:06,466
Don't listen to him,
he's just trying
to scare you.

1311
01:28:06,633 --> 01:28:09,010
No, I'm not trying
to scare you.
You're already scared.

1312
01:28:09,469 --> 01:28:11,137
I'm scared.

1313
01:28:13,765 --> 01:28:15,058
But I'd rather risk
my life out there

1314
01:28:15,141 --> 01:28:16,810
than spending the rest
of it in here.

1315
01:28:19,187 --> 01:28:21,189
We don't belong here.

1316
01:28:21,815 --> 01:28:24,526
This place isn't our home.

1317
01:28:25,443 --> 01:28:27,153
We were put here.

1318
01:28:27,529 --> 01:28:29,113
We were trapped here.

1319
01:28:30,824 --> 01:28:33,117
At least, out there
we have a choice.

1320
01:28:35,286 --> 01:28:37,372
We can make it
out of here.

1321
01:28:38,623 --> 01:28:39,666
I know that.

1322
01:28:53,012 --> 01:28:54,556
I'm sorry.

1323
01:29:08,319 --> 01:29:10,697
THOMAS: Gally, it's over.

1324
01:29:13,366 --> 01:29:15,869
Just come with us.

1325
01:29:23,543 --> 01:29:25,837
Good luck against
the Grievers.

1326
01:29:44,564 --> 01:29:46,107
THOMAS: Everybody,
this way!

1327
01:30:00,204 --> 01:30:02,123
Keep it up, guys,
we're almost there!

1328
01:30:10,924 --> 01:30:12,592
(GROWLING)

1329
01:30:16,471 --> 01:30:19,140
Is it a Griever?
Yeah.

1330
01:30:20,099 --> 01:30:21,392
Shit.

1331
01:30:21,809 --> 01:30:24,312
You take this, Chuck.
Stay behind us.

1332
01:30:26,397 --> 01:30:28,983
It's okay.
Just stick
with me.

1333
01:30:30,068 --> 01:30:31,569
Once we're through,
it will activate

1334
01:30:31,653 --> 01:30:32,946
and the door will open.

1335
01:30:33,112 --> 01:30:35,239
We stay close,
we stick together...

1336
01:30:35,406 --> 01:30:37,659
we get through this.
We get out now...

1337
01:30:37,825 --> 01:30:39,911
or we die trying.

1338
01:30:40,912 --> 01:30:41,996
Ready?

1339
01:30:43,456 --> 01:30:45,458
All right. Let's go!

1340
01:30:45,959 --> 01:30:47,627
(ALL YELLING)

1341
01:30:51,089 --> 01:30:52,423
(ROARING)

1342
01:30:52,840 --> 01:30:54,509
(ALL YELLING)

1343
01:31:00,932 --> 01:31:02,475
MINHO: Get up, look out!

1344
01:31:05,478 --> 01:31:06,479
Push it!

1345
01:31:11,985 --> 01:31:12,986
Look out!

1346
01:31:13,361 --> 01:31:14,362
(SCREAMING)

1347
01:31:16,447 --> 01:31:17,824
(ROARS)
(ALL GASP)

1348
01:31:22,078 --> 01:31:23,246
The key!

1349
01:31:23,413 --> 01:31:25,665
Chuck! Watch the edge!

1350
01:31:26,582 --> 01:31:27,750
(GRUNTING)

1351
01:31:29,127 --> 01:31:31,170
(SNARLING)

1352
01:31:32,505 --> 01:31:33,548
Oh, no.

1353
01:31:35,008 --> 01:31:36,926
I got you, Chuck!
Pull me up!

1354
01:31:39,679 --> 01:31:41,389
(ALL YELLING)

1355
01:31:44,851 --> 01:31:45,852
(ALL CHEERING)

1356
01:31:47,645 --> 01:31:48,771
TERESA: Come on!

1357
01:31:49,355 --> 01:31:51,691
Thomas! Thomas!

1358
01:31:52,275 --> 01:31:53,276
Chuck?

1359
01:31:53,443 --> 01:31:54,777
We got more coming!

1360
01:31:56,362 --> 01:31:58,364
Keep it steady, guys!

1361
01:31:59,032 --> 01:32:00,033
(KEY BEEPING)

1362
01:32:00,616 --> 01:32:01,701
It works!

1363
01:32:02,994 --> 01:32:04,871
(BOY SCREAMING)
Teresa, go!

1364
01:32:08,666 --> 01:32:11,044
THOMAS: Don't back down!
Keep pushing!
NEWT: Stay together!

1365
01:32:14,881 --> 01:32:15,882
(TERESA GRUNTS
IN FRUSTRATION)

1366
01:32:16,007 --> 01:32:17,550
There's gotta be
a way out! Come on!

1367
01:32:22,013 --> 01:32:23,014
(YELLS)

1368
01:32:25,224 --> 01:32:26,225
THOMAS: Watch it!

1369
01:32:26,517 --> 01:32:28,102
(SCREAMING)

1370
01:32:28,603 --> 01:32:29,812
(ROARING)

1371
01:32:31,564 --> 01:32:33,566
TERESA: It won't open!

1372
01:32:36,861 --> 01:32:39,197
Thomas!
There's a code!

1373
01:32:39,363 --> 01:32:40,406
Eight numbers!

1374
01:32:42,867 --> 01:32:44,202
Eight sections
of the maze.

1375
01:32:44,327 --> 01:32:47,330
Hey, Minho!
What's the sequence?
What?

1376
01:32:47,413 --> 01:32:49,248
The sections of the maze,
what's the sequence?

1377
01:32:50,541 --> 01:32:52,085
Seven! One!

1378
01:32:52,668 --> 01:32:54,253
Five! Two!

1379
01:32:54,420 --> 01:32:56,255
Six! Four!
Heads up!

1380
01:32:56,422 --> 01:32:57,423
(ROARING)

1381
01:32:58,925 --> 01:33:00,009
(SCREAMS)
NEWT: Minho!

1382
01:33:00,093 --> 01:33:01,094
THOMAS: Minho!
Oh!

1383
01:33:03,429 --> 01:33:04,847
(GRUNTING)
Get off of me!

1384
01:33:05,765 --> 01:33:06,766
(YELLS)

1385
01:33:08,309 --> 01:33:09,435
(GRUNTING)

1386
01:33:12,063 --> 01:33:13,064
(SCREAMING)

1387
01:33:14,607 --> 01:33:15,900
Jeff!

1388
01:33:16,067 --> 01:33:17,652
(CONTINUES SCREAMING)

1389
01:33:18,611 --> 01:33:19,862
What's the sequence?
Come on!

1390
01:33:20,238 --> 01:33:22,740
Six! Four! Eight!

1391
01:33:22,907 --> 01:33:24,450
Three! You got it?

1392
01:33:26,202 --> 01:33:27,620
THOMAS: Keep holding!

1393
01:33:27,912 --> 01:33:29,038
Almost there, come on!

1394
01:33:30,123 --> 01:33:31,207
BOY: The door opened!

1395
01:33:32,291 --> 01:33:33,501
(BOTH SCREECHING)

1396
01:33:34,752 --> 01:33:36,212
(BOYS SCREAMING)

1397
01:33:38,798 --> 01:33:40,133
(GRUNTS)
BOYS: Oh!

1398
01:33:42,802 --> 01:33:44,262
(ALL SIGHING IN RELIEF)

1399
01:33:44,345 --> 01:33:45,555
(ALL SCREAMING)

1400
01:34:58,211 --> 01:34:59,587
Seriously?

1401
01:35:43,339 --> 01:35:44,799
WINSTON: What happened here?

1402
01:36:18,791 --> 01:36:20,626
So they were watching us.

1403
01:36:21,836 --> 01:36:23,462
This whole time.

1404
01:36:49,196 --> 01:36:50,656
<i>Hello.</i>

1405
01:36:50,823 --> 01:36:52,992
<i>My name is
Doctor Ava Paige.</i>

1406
01:36:53,451 --> 01:36:54,910
<i>I'm Director
of Operations</i>

1407
01:36:54,994 --> 01:36:58,372
<i>of the World Catastrophe
Killzone Department.</i>

1408
01:36:58,539 --> 01:36:59,957
<i>If you're watching this,
that means</i>

1409
01:37:00,041 --> 01:37:03,002
<i>you have successfully
completed the Maze Trials.</i>

1410
01:37:03,502 --> 01:37:06,630
<i>I wish I could
be there in person
to congratulate you...</i>

1411
01:37:08,341 --> 01:37:12,178
<i>but circumstances seem
to have prevented it.</i>

1412
01:37:12,345 --> 01:37:14,847
<i>I'm sure by now,
you must all be
very confused...</i>

1413
01:37:15,681 --> 01:37:16,724
<i>angry...</i>

1414
01:37:16,891 --> 01:37:18,392
<i>frightened.</i>

1415
01:37:18,559 --> 01:37:21,687
<i>I can only assure you,
that everything
that's happened to you...</i>

1416
01:37:22,688 --> 01:37:25,149
<i>everything we've done
to you...</i>

1417
01:37:25,316 --> 01:37:27,360
<i>it was all done
for a reason.</i>

1418
01:37:28,027 --> 01:37:29,737
<i>You won't remember...</i>

1419
01:37:29,904 --> 01:37:32,656
<i>but the Sun has
scorched our world.</i>

1420
01:37:34,492 --> 01:37:36,994
<i>Billions of lives
lost to fire...</i>

1421
01:37:37,870 --> 01:37:38,871
<i>famine...</i>

1422
01:37:39,372 --> 01:37:42,333
<i>suffering
on a global scale.</i>

1423
01:37:42,500 --> 01:37:45,503
<i>The fallout
was unimaginable.</i>

1424
01:37:46,253 --> 01:37:48,881
<i>What came after was worse.</i>

1425
01:37:49,715 --> 01:37:51,217
<i>We called it the Flare.</i>

1426
01:37:52,385 --> 01:37:55,805
<i>A deadly virus that
attacks the brain.</i>

1427
01:37:55,971 --> 01:37:57,807
<i>It is violent...</i>

1428
01:37:57,973 --> 01:37:59,517
<i>unpredictable...</i>

1429
01:38:00,351 --> 01:38:02,228
<i>incurable.</i>

1430
01:38:03,521 --> 01:38:05,064
<i>Or so we thought.</i>

1431
01:38:06,732 --> 01:38:09,110
<i>In time, a new
generation emerged</i>

1432
01:38:09,193 --> 01:38:10,986
<i>that could survive
the virus.</i>

1433
01:38:11,153 --> 01:38:14,657
<i>Suddenly, there was
a reason to hope
for a cure.</i>

1434
01:38:16,033 --> 01:38:18,577
<i>But finding it
would not be easy.</i>

1435
01:38:18,744 --> 01:38:21,872
<i>The young would
have to be tested,
even sacrificed...</i>

1436
01:38:22,206 --> 01:38:24,375
<i>inside harsh environments...</i>

1437
01:38:24,542 --> 01:38:26,585
<i>where their brain activity
could be studied.</i>

1438
01:38:27,503 --> 01:38:29,046
<i>All in an effort
to understand...</i>

1439
01:38:29,213 --> 01:38:31,382
<i>what makes them different...</i>

1440
01:38:32,591 --> 01:38:35,428
<i>what makes you different.</i>

1441
01:38:36,679 --> 01:38:38,681
<i>You may not realize it...</i>

1442
01:38:38,848 --> 01:38:41,225
<i>but you're very important.</i>

1443
01:38:41,600 --> 01:38:44,437
<i>Unfortunately, your trials
have only just begun.</i>

1444
01:38:44,603 --> 01:38:46,605
<i>As you will no doubt
soon discover,</i>

1445
01:38:46,689 --> 01:38:48,774
<i>not everyone agrees
with our methods.</i>

1446
01:38:48,941 --> 01:38:52,111
<i>Progress is slow,
people are scared.</i>

1447
01:38:52,278 --> 01:38:54,864
<i>It may be too late for us...</i>

1448
01:38:54,947 --> 01:38:56,782
<i>for me...</i>

1449
01:38:56,949 --> 01:38:58,284
<i>but not for you.</i>

1450
01:38:59,201 --> 01:39:01,036
<i>The outside world awaits.</i>

1451
01:39:01,620 --> 01:39:03,038
<i>Remember...</i>

1452
01:39:06,459 --> 01:39:07,918
<i>Wicked is good.</i>

1453
01:39:08,961 --> 01:39:10,296
(GUNSHOT)

1454
01:39:33,694 --> 01:39:34,695
(DOOR OPENING)

1455
01:39:43,662 --> 01:39:45,164
Is it over?

1456
01:39:46,999 --> 01:39:48,959
She said we were
important.

1457
01:39:50,669 --> 01:39:52,630
What are we
supposed
to do now?

1458
01:40:01,263 --> 01:40:02,848
I don't know.

1459
01:40:08,270 --> 01:40:10,022
Let's get out of here.

1460
01:40:12,691 --> 01:40:13,692
GALLY: No.

1461
01:40:18,447 --> 01:40:20,032
Gally?
Don't.

1462
01:40:21,158 --> 01:40:22,952
He's been stung.

1463
01:40:27,706 --> 01:40:28,791
(SNIFFLES)

1464
01:40:30,543 --> 01:40:31,877
We can't leave.

1465
01:40:35,839 --> 01:40:37,883
We did.
Gally, we're out.

1466
01:40:39,009 --> 01:40:40,302
We're free.

1467
01:40:42,638 --> 01:40:43,806
Free?

1468
01:40:47,309 --> 01:40:49,311
You think we're
free out there?

1469
01:40:50,563 --> 01:40:51,730
No.

1470
01:40:53,899 --> 01:40:56,193
No, there's no escape
from this place.

1471
01:41:01,365 --> 01:41:02,825
Gally, listen to me.

1472
01:41:02,992 --> 01:41:05,244
You're not
thinking straight.

1473
01:41:05,869 --> 01:41:07,037
You're not.

1474
01:41:07,913 --> 01:41:09,915
Now, we can help you.

1475
01:41:11,417 --> 01:41:13,419
Just put down the gun.

1476
01:41:14,211 --> 01:41:15,921
I belong to the maze.

1477
01:41:16,088 --> 01:41:17,840
THOMAS: Just put down
the gun.

1478
01:41:20,884 --> 01:41:22,261
We all do.

1479
01:41:25,347 --> 01:41:26,599
(GALLY WHEEZING)

1480
01:41:26,682 --> 01:41:27,766
(KEY CLATTERING)

1481
01:41:28,601 --> 01:41:30,352
(GASPS)

1482
01:41:43,115 --> 01:41:44,408
Thomas...

1483
01:41:46,285 --> 01:41:47,703
Chuck.
(GROANING)

1484
01:41:52,374 --> 01:41:54,209
Oh, shit. Shit.

1485
01:41:55,294 --> 01:41:56,629
Look at me,
look at me!

1486
01:41:57,963 --> 01:41:58,964
Oh, shit!
(WHIMPERING)

1487
01:41:59,131 --> 01:42:00,633
THOMAS: Chuck,
look at me, all right?

1488
01:42:00,924 --> 01:42:02,301
I got you, buddy.
Just hang on.

1489
01:42:02,885 --> 01:42:04,303
It's okay.

1490
01:42:04,637 --> 01:42:06,138
Thomas, Thomas...

1491
01:42:11,602 --> 01:42:13,604
No, Chuck.
You're gonna give
it to them yourself.

1492
01:42:13,771 --> 01:42:14,772
Remember,
I told you that.

1493
01:42:14,897 --> 01:42:16,148
Take it.

1494
01:42:16,815 --> 01:42:17,941
THOMAS: No.

1495
01:42:20,486 --> 01:42:21,487
Thank you.

1496
01:42:25,491 --> 01:42:26,659
Thank you.

1497
01:42:26,992 --> 01:42:28,118
No, Chuck,
you're gonna get...

1498
01:42:28,202 --> 01:42:29,495
(GROANS SOFTLY)

1499
01:42:30,371 --> 01:42:31,372
(EXHALES)

1500
01:42:32,831 --> 01:42:33,832
Chuck.

1501
01:42:36,585 --> 01:42:38,170
Chuck? Hey.

1502
01:42:40,089 --> 01:42:41,840
Hey, Chuck, come on!

1503
01:42:42,800 --> 01:42:44,385
Come on, wake up!

1504
01:42:46,345 --> 01:42:48,013
(SOBBING)

1505
01:42:52,184 --> 01:42:53,185
THOMAS: Damn it!

1506
01:42:56,146 --> 01:42:58,065
(SOBBING) We made it.
Come on.

1507
01:43:03,112 --> 01:43:04,780
I'm sorry!

1508
01:43:06,031 --> 01:43:07,324
God damn it!
(DOORS OPENING)

1509
01:43:08,867 --> 01:43:10,703
Damn it!

1510
01:43:11,036 --> 01:43:12,371
(THOMAS CONTINUES SOBBING)

1511
01:43:16,792 --> 01:43:17,876
Thomas.
THOMAS: Chuck!

1512
01:43:21,588 --> 01:43:23,799
Get up, Chuck! Come on!

1513
01:43:24,466 --> 01:43:25,968
(HOODED MEN SHOUTING)

1514
01:43:36,937 --> 01:43:38,021
THOMAS: Chuck!

1515
01:43:39,606 --> 01:43:41,525
You can't just
leave him there!

1516
01:44:19,396 --> 01:44:20,606
You guys all right?

1517
01:44:21,356 --> 01:44:22,483
Don't worry.

1518
01:44:22,649 --> 01:44:24,026
You're safe now.

1519
01:45:00,604 --> 01:45:02,189
Relax, kid.

1520
01:45:03,565 --> 01:45:05,901
Everything is gonna change.

1521
01:45:20,749 --> 01:45:24,002
I think it's safe to say
the Maze Trials were
a complete success.

1522
01:45:25,712 --> 01:45:28,048
<i>I wasn't expecting
so many survivors, but...</i>

1523
01:45:29,091 --> 01:45:30,342
<i>the more the merrier.</i>

1524
01:45:34,805 --> 01:45:38,517
<i>Thomas continues to
surprise and impress.</i>

1525
01:45:39,852 --> 01:45:43,605
<i>And for now, they seem
to have taken the bait.</i>

1526
01:45:44,731 --> 01:45:46,650
<i>It's too soon to say...</i>

1527
01:45:48,360 --> 01:45:50,487
<i>but they could be
the key to everything.</i>

1528
01:45:53,323 --> 01:45:54,700
<i>So let's move forward.</i>

1529
01:45:56,451 --> 01:45:59,538
It's time now
to begin Phase Two.

